{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel","id":1475101,"title":"Canonical Garou vs Vampire elder duel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-21T06:25:52-08:00","id":1475101,"title":"Canonical Garou vs Vampire elder duel","content":"Hi there.<br /> The title speak for itself. I always find it frustrating that Garou got their asses kicked everytime they fight vampire Elder (Mitra, Yaga, etc.) They seems to be able only to not-really-sucssesful zerg-rushes (again, Mithra). Was there any canonical 1-to-1 fight between vampire and Garou elder,s with convincing victory of the latter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T06:46:52-08:00","id":1475103,"title":"","content":"I can't recall. Also, Mitra and especially Baba Yaga, are Methuselah, well beyond an Elder vampire. Depending on what you thing of the non-canon &quot;Masquerade of the Red Death&quot; novels, Baba Yaga might not have been human before the Embrace...<br /> <br /> With all their might, Elder Garou (Rank 5) or even Legends (Rank 6) are still mortals. Vampires of generations below the 8th, with sufficient age and discipline dots at their disposal, are basically demi-gods. There surely have been successful attacks of garou on Elder vampires, but I can't recall a specific fight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T09:09:52-08:00","id":1475113,"title":"","content":"Canon has few. One Silent Strider (with aid of a kinfolk sorcerer) defeat Set, but the whole tribe was cursed and that magician was embraced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T10:35:30-08:00","id":1475119,"title":"","content":"Canonical? I don't think there are.<br /> <br /> There are two major reasons for this decision by the authors, I think. The first is that the trope that Elder Vampires are on a whole other level is too strong, regardless of how much it is backed by the rules (and it is to an extend). The second is the idea that a centuries- or millennia-old vampire will be prepared by default (which is also true to an extend).<br /> <br /> It certainly should have examples. Even those vampires commit mistakes and werewolves can prepare good plans. But at the end of the day the authors simply didn't found the need to make an example of that yet.<br /> <br /> But there are nuances to this that are important. First that an Elder vampire, especially if you're using each line's proper rules, really isn't a fair fight for most Garou. Not because of potential power, but because of expected dot distribution for the <i>typical</i> character. You can make an Elder Garou with the sheet to go face-to-face with an Elder Vampire and win, but if you work with average expectations for the setting (which you should when making canonical material) the <b>Elder</b> vampire will likely have more dots invested in things that will benefit in this particular encounter than the Elder Garou, as a result of how their respective power sets work (having access to 5th level, sometimes even 6th, from the get go helps a lot) and how their societies work (vampires are more focused on being personally able to handle threats to their survival instead of trusting mates).<br /> <br /> Another thing is just how often such clashes happen at all. While the Garou is oriented to do battle, the vampire is oriented to avoid it, even more so if an Elder. When you achieve a major victory against them it means you pierced a lot of machinations and destroyed the ongoing corruption. Instead of staying there to face you and protect their stuff with their power, though, even if they think they have the advantage, Elder Vampires are more likely to just get the fuck out of Dodge and lick their wounded egos elsewhere far away from you.<br /> <br /> Finally, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> pointed out, the likes of Mythras aren't Elders, but Methuselah. While they're still vampires, their role in the setting is more akin to that of Incarnae, both in influence and in raw power. Sasha Vykos and Lucita are powerful Elders, very powerful, and yet still far beneath that.<br /> <br /> So in the end it is understandably easier for the authors to write about young werewolves thinking an Elder vampire is a piece of cake to fight and having their asses served than to write about a direct duel between two Elders of both lines. By the way, writing about two Elders or Elder-equivalent of any two lines coming to blows is generally a tricky proposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T10:38:16-08:00","id":1475120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475113#post1475113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canon has few. One Silent Strider (with aid of a kinfolk sorcerer) defeat Set, but the whole tribe was cursed and that magician was embraced</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T10:42:16-08:00","id":1475121,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, finding and killing any vampire during the day is also not really a fun story to read.<br /> And if the garou do not happen to find a vampire elder by chance, but actually search for one and plan an assault on the haven during the day, the situation might be very different...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T10:52:04-08:00","id":1475123,"title":"","content":"And that's why Gadou are defected spice of old WoD.<br /> Shame!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 02-21-2022, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:02:45-08:00","id":1475126,"title":"","content":"It would be an entire Garou pack against a Kindred elder, not just one on one (Garou don\u2019t care about fair play when fighting Leeches). And yes, the Garou could win in this scenario, but they would probably take a few casualties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:08:19-08:00","id":1475128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475126#post1475126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be an entire Garou pack against a Kindred elder, not just one on one (Garou don\u2019t care about fair play when fighting Leeches). And yes, the Garou could win in this scenario, but they would probably take a few casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why Gadou are defected spice of old WoD.<br /> Shame!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:41:09-08:00","id":1475133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475126#post1475126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be an entire Garou pack against a Kindred elder, not just one on one (Garou don\u2019t care about fair play when fighting Leeches). And yes, the Garou could win in this scenario, but they would probably take a few casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> Elder Garou also have a lot of supernatural resources they can use other possible sources of advantages that are harder for a vampire to get. An Elder Garou fixated on the task and with some days to prepare for it is certainly capable of defeating an Elder Vampire in duel (lets not say a fair fight because none of the two would actually be playing fair. And if it was, mostly it would hold true). If they have the benefit of daylight, it will probably be easy (it may not be, but then depends on too much specifics).<br /> <br /> The problem isn't if it can happen in theory. It is if you can write a good and compelling story out of it that benefits the setting as a whole after considering the context in which it will happen, and that the writers simply concluded they don't have such a story to tell yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:49:18-08:00","id":1475134,"title":"","content":"There's also an issue where vampires have always gotten the plot armor in the canon of the wider WoD, because VtM was the original game and the biggest game for most of its history. Jonas and Cyrus aren't allowed to join forces and use the turmoil in Chicago to take out a bunch of vampires when the timing is great, because that would mean a bunch of fan favorite VtM NPCs would get offed. When VtM needs to show off how potent the higher powered vampires really are, whole Septs get wiped out (and the rural bias of the Garou means that it's easy to avoid any of the big name NPCs). Mage has suffered a similar fate when it comes to the canon of the WoD (though at least they get a few &quot;wins&quot; in the vampire is supposed to lose).<br /> <br /> Even for all the power a Gen 5 Methuselah can bring to bare, they're not actually unbeatable: we have stats for some of them. A Legendary Garou using all their own resources (Garou have politics, connections, and so on as well) can easily - if you go by the rules in the books - come out on top. But the fiction comes first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T11:58:25-08:00","id":1475135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475134#post1475134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also an issue where vampires have always gotten the plot armor in the canon of the wider WoD, because VtM was the original game and the biggest game for most of its history. Jonas and Cyrus aren't allowed to join forces and use the turmoil in Chicago to take out a bunch of vampires when the timing is great, because that would mean a bunch of fan favorite VtM NPCs would get offed. When VtM needs to show off how potent the higher powered vampires really are, whole Septs get wiped out (and the rural bias of the Garou means that it's easy to avoid any of the big name NPCs). Mage has suffered a similar fate when it comes to the canon of the WoD (though at least they get a few &amp;quot;wins&amp;quot; in the vampire is supposed to lose).<br /> <br /> Even for all the power a Gen 5 Methuselah can bring to bare, they're not actually unbeatable: we have stats for some of them. A Legendary Garou using all their own resources (Garou have politics, connections, and so on as well) can easily - if you go by the rules in the books - come out on top. But the fiction comes first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And thank's to this fiction - Garou are second-class spices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T12:44:18-08:00","id":1475137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475135#post1475135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. And thank's to this fiction - Garou are second-class spices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure what precisely you mean by that, or if I agree at all. But repeating it <i>ad nauseam</i> isn't making it clearer, just annoying.<br /> <br /> First of all, crossover fiction is a thing, but not the most common type of thing. So this is a concern about very specific texts and not a general depiction of the setting.<br /> <br /> Second, fights between important NPCs where life is at stake aren't something to be done lightly and are generally avoided, regardless.<br /> <br /> Third, almost every story involving a Werewolf begins with some sort of statement that they're expected to win a fight by default. How's that being a second-class something when you're the literal gold standard for badassery?<br /> <br /> And forth, Werewolves are already the splat that more frequently fights other things than their equals, up to and including beings that are explicitly above their league, are in talking terms with actual gods, and can take all of that for granted.<br /> <br /> Literally they're the most obvious target to showcase the strength of a character in fiction because they're the most dangerous target by far as a base premise. This is easy storytelling, certainly, but no less true.<br /> <br /> You can and should complain that crossover fiction likes too much to punch Werewolves to show how others are strong. This is true and cheap, and the sheer frequency ends up reversing the message to a degree. But to say they're second class when they're the guys everyone else without exception use as bogeymen and avoid like death incarnate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T12:55:38-08:00","id":1475140,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole spice thing is... weird at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475137#post1475137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, almost every story involving a Werewolf begins with some sort of statement that they're expected to win a fight by default. How's that being a second-class something when you're the literal gold standard for badassery?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the Garou are the Worfs of the WoD. They get talked about how dangerous and badass they are, but we never get to see it in the crossover fiction of the WoD, where they usually get their butts handed to them to show how powerful something else is (generally an ancient vampire, maybe the Technocracy, at least once both).<br /> <br /> Also vampires are the only WoD supernaturals that are consistent in seeing Lupines as unstoppable murder machines of nightmare (also, again a legacy of book order), as most of the other games either don't interact with them in a meaningful way, have factions that have more positive interactions with them, or - whether true or not - think they should be considered scarier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T13:23:06-08:00","id":1475143,"title":"","content":"In Vampire: Bloodlines the werewolf is basically a killing machine and unstoppable, except for a trick...<br /> <br /> On the other hand one of Moonstone comics showed garou in cages within the succubus club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:04:57-08:00","id":1475145,"title":"","content":"VtM:B is hardly representative of a lot of things. Though the werewolf attack: (1) fails to kill Nines who is one of the main targets (2) the only goal is to survive, which you can do by just avoiding the werewolf for long enough, (3) for all the main character does in a ridiculously short amount of time, the main character is hardly presented as how badass vampires can be... and can kill a werewolf by being smart about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:56:11-08:00","id":1475152,"title":"","content":"I assume our friend means &quot;species,&quot; but beyond that everyone else is on their own.<br /> <br /> I've always liked the Lupine encounter in Bloodlines; it instills the amount of panic that a Kindred would have (until you figure the encounter's mechanics out), and Nines sending you to kill the other bosses after he's handled a Lupine on his own strikes just the right cynical note - this older and more powerful Kindred considers the final battle too dangerous for himself, so it's time once again for the player to do another vampire's shit work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T17:07:05-08:00","id":1475159,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Mithras acting as a flesh-car for one of the Earthbound? Not really representative, if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T17:47:14-08:00","id":1475163,"title":"","content":"No, but the confusion is deliberate. Asmodeus disguised his cult of worshippers as a Mithras cult to influence the Roman emperor, Constantine. That all went to crap for Asmodeus when Constantine changed his religious affiliation.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, there's no hint of that cult ever crossing paths with the cult of the same name that the Ventrue Methusaleh cultivated around himself, but that's probably due to the pronounced lack of overlap between V:tM and D:tF in official sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 02-21-2022, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T18:44:22-08:00","id":1475166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475137#post1475137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure what precisely you mean by that, or if I agree at all. But repeating it <i>ad nauseam</i> isn't making it clearer, just annoying.<br /> <br /> First of all, crossover fiction is a thing, but not the most common type of thing. So this is a concern about very specific texts and not a general depiction of the setting.<br /> <br /> Second, fights between important NPCs where life is at stake aren't something to be done lightly and are generally avoided, regardless.<br /> <br /> Third, almost every story involving a Werewolf begins with some sort of statement that they're expected to win a fight by default. How's that being a second-class something when you're the literal gold standard for badassery?<br /> <br /> And forth, Werewolves are already the splat that more frequently fights other things than their equals, up to and including beings that are explicitly above their league, are in talking terms with actual gods, and can take all of that for granted.<br /> <br /> Literally they're the most obvious target to showcase the strength of a character in fiction because they're the most dangerous target by far as a base premise. This is easy storytelling, certainly, but no less true.<br /> <br /> You can and should complain that crossover fiction likes too much to punch Werewolves to show how others are strong. This is true and cheap, and the sheer frequency ends up reversing the message to a degree. But to say they're second class when they're the guys everyone else without exception use as bogeymen and avoid like death incarnate?</div> </div> </div> </div>So Onyx Pathe essentually assert gamelines at WtA expense. And demote Garou to biggest loosers of WoD, who only exist to be humilated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T19:23:03-08:00","id":1475170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475120#post1475120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a page reference....</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, history section of two editions\u2019 Silent Strider book. 1st introduces that guy, Shu-Horus. He did defeat Set and did make him unmovable until Gehenna, but cost is terribly high<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shu Heru (Shu Horus)<br /> Striders all across the globe revere the ancient Egyptian Shu Heru, who led the tribe into its exile. Although his name is all-too-often remembered in the tongues of the conquerors, he is hailed as the mightiest Strider in peace and in war. He counseled his tribe to treat with the mummies when they were first born, and he was one of the few Garou leaders to establish a temporary truce with Bastet and Mokol\u00e9 alike. He also was a proven slayer of the hot-blooded vampires of ancient times, and destroyed almost countless childer of Set. Shu Horus even eventually did battle against the Antediluvian himself, Set the Ruler, Set the Usurper.<br /> Alas, he and the tribe were cursed for their pains, and Set could hardly have put a greater doom on the defiant Striders. Yet Shu Heru's strength was so great that even in his tribe's darkest hour, he was able to lead them to their new lives. Although most tales of Shu Horus end with his tribe's exile, Strider Galliards know that his deeds of valor did not end when he forever left the land of Khem.<br /> It is unrecorded where and when this legend among Garou died. And even today, his descendants and tribesfolk curse Set's name, for the ancient vampire's malison caused no greater ill than severing the Silent Striders from the guiding spirit of their greatest hero.<br /> <br /> WW3059 Page 65 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T21:28:37-08:00","id":1475182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475140#post1475140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the Garou are the Worfs of the WoD. They get talked about how dangerous and badass they are, but we never get to see it in the crossover fiction of the WoD, where they usually get their butts handed to them to show how powerful something else is (generally an ancient vampire, maybe the Technocracy, at least once both).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as I said it is cheap storytelling, the Worf Effect is in full blown with them, sometimes with some Conservation of Ninjutsu applied, which makes no sense for Werewolves at all. This isn't even exclusive to other lines, as W:tA does this with other Fera more frequently than it should.<br /> <br /> In the end things are a lot more complex. Everyone but Vampires tend to talk from a perspective of superiority to everything else, even though vampires aren't actually as weak in comparison, but as a rule of thumb everyone recognizes Werewolves as dangerous in combat. Other splats are just confident in being able to either avoid or outsmart them.<br /> <br /> And the final problem is that the same way the authors in other lines have a tendency to greatly overestimate their strength in battle (until Worf Effect kicks in), they also have the same tendency to greatly underestimate their ability to be a complete and complex splat with other resources, strengths and strategies to deal with things. They are <b><u>not</u></b> just glorified chainsaws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475143#post1475143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Vampire: Bloodlines the werewolf is basically a killing machine and unstoppable, except for a trick...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is how many players think it is or should be, but is one of the many moments in that game that doesn't really convey how things actually work in the game.<br /> <br /> In the end that battle works as a storytelling device for the game, but it is still completely off in the greater context of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475166#post1475166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Onyx Pathe essentually assert gamelines at WtA expense. And demote Garou to biggest loosers of WoD, who only exist to be humilated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you did meant something similar to what I thought.<br /> <br /> And this isn't quite like that in many ways. First that it wasn't Onyx Path most of the time, I think most fiction with this characteristic is from WW's time. WoD isn't an OPP product, they just work on X20 lines, and most fiction that I know of is older than that. Other can correct me if I'm wrong, I'm not really taking notes of everything released and rarely bother with novels.<br /> <br /> Second, as we already said here, saying that they only exist to be humiliated or that other lines are asserted at their expense is greatly, <b>hugely</b> overstating this.<br /> <br /> <b>Characters are asserted with this. <u>Lines not</u>.</b> Each and every splat in the WoD knows that facing Werewolves head on is a dumb idea, period. This is repeated in variable, but no uncertain terms every time. Most have reason to not be too bothered by this, but that's because they don't expect conflict to be unavoidable for one reason or another. Not fearing the fighter because you're confident in avoiding the fight is not the same as thinking you're stronger. Some also <u><b>can be</b></u> formidable foes on their own, but then they're recognizing that they need their best to be able to take on a Werewolf. <b><i>Again, by default</i></b>.<br /> <br /> I do agree that they receive a fairly bad treatment in crossovers, but we're talking a setting were crossovers are a niche thing to begin with, and where that happens precisely because they're the most meaningful foe to show how much a given character is <i><b>powerful beyond the measure of their kind</b></i>, while you can hardly show that for Werewolf characters pitting them against other splats.<br /> <br /> Remember that pitting important NPCs against one another in a live-or-die scenario is a no-go, and strong characters are usually also important even to be recognized as such. Mithras killing a whole Sept shows he is extremely powerful. Albretch killing a whole Elysium shows it is Thursday. <b>Albretch facing Mithras won't happen, because they won't sacrifice one for the sake of showing of the other</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T21:57:16-08:00","id":1475187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475182#post1475182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that pitting important NPCs against one another in a live-or-die scenario is a no-go, and strong characters are usually also important even to be recognized as such. Mithras killing a whole Sept shows he is extremely powerful. Albretch killing a whole Elysium shows it is Thursday. <b>Albretch facing Mithras won't happen, because they won't sacrifice one for the sake of showing of the other</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could show this Thuesday just at once. Or mention some dispossable John Doe-elder who was killed by Albreht to show, how badass Albreht is. Coise now, it't only make sense for to play a Garou who join Wyrm for sake of more-power. Aftdr all, Ramsy Bolton always will be a greater character than Robb Stark.<br /> P.S. I'm glad nWoD werewolves, while still badass, were reasonably nerfed. If Onyx Path'll someday decide to develope 'canon' timeline, it's Beasts or Demons who gonna be Worfs there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T22:06:57-08:00","id":1475188,"title":"","content":"You keep saying Onyx Path... Onyx Path doesn't (and has never) owned the WoD or CofD. Anything they do needs approval from the current IP owners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T22:19:03-08:00","id":1475189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475187#post1475187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could show this Thuesday just at once. Or mention some dispossable John Doe-elder who was killed by Albreht to show, how badass Albreht is. Coise now, it't only make sense for to play a Garou who join Wyrm for sake of more-power. Aftdr all, Ramsy Bolton always will be a greater character than Robb Stark.<br /> P.S. I'm glad nWoD werewolves, while still badass, were reasonably nerfed. If Onyx Path'll someday decide to develope 'canon' timeline, it's Beasts or Demons who gonna be Worfs there.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could and should. It's far trickier than you seem to think, but it is also certainly withing their purview. I just think you're jumping to a lot of conclusions from this.<br /> <br /> Joining the Wyrm for more power? No amount of proper badassery will change that joining the Wyrm is the easiest path for power, because that's kind of the point. And while incredibly strong Werewolves aren't meant to face their worse foes alone, they're pack fighters.<br /> <br /> You seem excessively focused on individual strength as a means to validate a character, and that's not quite how this setting works outside a few cases. Hence the problem being real, but I don't think it is near the proportion you give it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T22:43:52-08:00","id":1475191,"title":"","content":"Vampires that live long enough to be an elder generally aren't going to fight you unless they are confident the deck is stacked in their favor to an obscene extent, against anyone strong enough to be the slightest threat their natural instinct is to run away without a hint of shame over ducking the fight. Alternatively, they royally screw it up and you manage to catch them while they are in torpor or something but nobody really considers ganking a person in a coma to be a statement of combat prowess worth bragging about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T23:40:43-08:00","id":1475196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475170#post1475170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, history section of two editions\u2019 Silent Strider book. 1st introduces that guy, Shu-Horus. He did defeat Set and did make him unmovable until Gehenna, but cost is terribly high</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I never read it as he, personally and alone (except for kinfolk sorcerer aid) did fight the Antedeluvian, but that the attack was a coordinated one, with other garou and other fera, mummies and sorcerers taking part...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T23:47:03-08:00","id":1475197,"title":"","content":"About the punching bag situation: V5 Chicago has vampires who hunt lupines as modus operandi and get the two Caerns (Fanum and ?) of that city destroyed as a sidenote...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T23:59:03-08:00","id":1475200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475191#post1475191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, they royally screw it up and you manage to catch them while they are in torpor or something but nobody really considers ganking a person in a coma to be a statement of combat prowess worth bragging about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, finding the vampire, bypassing security and traps, ghouls and things like that, might be a statement of one's detective qualities. Showing Wisdom, or for shifters who use that trait, Cunning.<br /> <br /> Thing is, that during 1st and parts of 2nd Edition Vampires were often regarded as a necessary evil. The are easily to kill, but annoying to hunt. With BSD, banes and formori spreading the Wyrm to far greater extend then a Masquerade-abiding Vampire, the garou rarely focus on vampires as their enemies. With the vampires themselves avoiding direct confrontation, clashes of some magnitude are potentially rare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T00:18:29-08:00","id":1475202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475197#post1475197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the punching bag situation: V5 Chicago has vampires who hunt lupines as modus operandi and get the two Caerns (Fanum and ?) of that city destroyed as a sidenote...</div> </div> </div> </div>See? I don't know why WW hate Garou that much, but it seems the LOVE to humilate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T00:52:38-08:00","id":1475203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475187#post1475187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aftdr all, Ramsy Bolton always will be a greater character than Robb Stark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm picking a somewhat random and petty point to jump in here.<br /> <br /> But says who?<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a books-versus-show point, and I am missing something as someone who has only seen the show, but Ramsay is not really a more interesting character than Robb Stark. Robb Stark just died earlier. Robb's story, someone who stuck to his principles even when he knew it wasn't the pragmatic choice, and died for it, is just as interesting (if not more) than Ramsay, whose story is essentially just an inferiority complex due to his bastard status plus sadism, which is still arguably just an expression of his inferiority complex combined with his relation to a house defined by cruelty. The fact that Ramsay died in a later season than Robb does not automatically make him a better character. That logic only holds up if you're measuring things purely by a survival/who-is-more-badass mentality. And again, it's very arguable, since we never got to see Ramsay fight Robb, and what circumstances a character survives versus what kills them are far bigger than who-is-more-badass as an individual.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that cWoD cares less about balance across gamelines and more about the themes of each gameline without considering crossover. The average Werewolf is way more badass than the average Vampire, but the exceptional Vampire tends to be more badass than the exceptional Werewolf (ignoring the points made above about how it's significantly muddier when you measure mechanics vs. fluff). And that's because the Vampire gameline was set up around the idea that elder or ancient Vampires are a force of nature compared to their younger kin, whereas Garou are more like regular people when you try to compare the average to the exceptional: they are awesome, but they aren't on a fundamentally different level when it comes to raw power or experience, because they are mortal and they eventually die of old age in the rare cases where they don't die in battle.<br /> <br /> Being a Vampire is all about biding your time and building up your power base, both personal and political, as long as possible without actively seeking out dangerous challenges to your position, with the idea that those that are able to keep playing this game for the long-term end up on a radically different level from those who are just beginning <b>if</b> they can survive for centuries or <b>millennia</b>.<br /> <br /> Being a Werewolf is about constantly throwing yourself against enemies that are a legitimate threat to your very survival, and not being respected by your peers unless you constantly put your life on the line.<br /> <br /> The stories that the Vampire and Werewolf gamelines are trying to tell are fundamentally different. In the Werewolf gameline, the overwhelming threat that makes the plot fundamentally grimdark is a corrupted cosmic force/deity that seeks to destroy everything that even remotely &quot;normal&quot; beings hold dear.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, the overwhelming threat is older Vampires, the Antediluvians being the most extreme example.<br /> <br /> The degree to which Elders and Methuselahs are radically more powerful than the average Vampire, or the average Werewolf, is because ancient Vampires in their gameline fill the role that powerful Jagglings or even Incarna fill within the Werewolf gameline: the overwhelming force that shapes the plot and makes it a story of horror or struggle rather than an optimistic fantasy adventure.<br /> <br /> And, to bring it back around to the original point, &quot;who is the better character&quot; in this case is not a question of who can survive better or who can punch harder. It's the question of what kind of story you enjoy; one that provokes powerful feelings, or produces interesting ideas. The Werewolf story is defined by an impossible struggle against an overwhelming enemy in the form of a corrupted cosmic force of destruction, and having demigod-like Werewolves undermines the themes of that story. Whereas the Vampire story is defined by demigod-like Vampires that effectively fill the function played by a corrupted cosmic force in the Werewolf story.<br /> <br /> To reduce it to the simplest expression, it's an apples-to-oranges comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T01:14:49-08:00","id":1475206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475203#post1475203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'm picking a somewhat random and petty point to jump in here.<br /> <br /> But says who?<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a books-versus-show point, and I am missing something as someone who has only seen the show, but Ramsay is not really a more interesting character than Robb Stark. Robb Stark just died earlier. Robb's story, someone who stuck to his principles even when he knew it wasn't the pragmatic choice, and died for it, is just as interesting (if not more) than Ramsay, whose story is essentially just an inferiority complex due to his bastard status plus sadism, which is still arguably just an expression of his inferiority complex combined with his relation to a house defined by cruelty. The fact that Ramsay died in a late