re fundamentally different. In the Werewolf gameline, the overwhelming threat that makes the plot fundamentally grimdark is a corrupted cosmic force/deity that seeks to destroy everything that even remotely &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; beings hold dear.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, the overwhelming threat is older Vampires, the Antediluvians being the most extreme example.<br /> <br /> The degree to which Elders and Methuselahs are radically more powerful than the average Vampire, or the average Werewolf, is because ancient Vampires in their gameline fill the role that powerful Jagglings or even Incarna fill within the Werewolf gameline: the overwhelming force that shapes the plot and makes it a story of horror or struggle rather than an optimistic fantasy adventure.<br /> <br /> And, to bring it back around to the original point, &amp;quot;who is the better character&amp;quot; in this case is not a question of who can survive better or who can punch harder. It's the question of what kind of story you enjoy; one that provokes powerful feelings, or produces interesting ideas. The Werewolf story is defined by an impossible struggle against an overwhelming enemy in the form of a corrupted cosmic force of destruction, and having demigod-like Werewolves undermines the themes of that story. Whereas the Vampire story is defined by demigod-like Vampires that effectively fill the function played by a corrupted cosmic force in the Werewolf story.<br /> <br /> To reduce it to the simplest expression, it's an apples-to-oranges comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's toiching approach... Tbh, I mean Ramsay is better character exactly couse of all the lives he ruined and all the evil he bring.... like someone who FORCED the world remember him. Although book!Ramsey's much dumber and less charismatic. Book!Euron, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> As for gamelines... well looking at large scale it means that vamps are way more awesome kind, than inferior Garou, becouse they can evolve into monsters no Garou hero can match, nevermind how epic he is. Again, cudos for CofD sinse elder werewolves had a (a vague) chance to evolve into something more epic. I just don't care about morality) &quot;Good, bad, I'm the guy with a gun&quot;)) <br /> Hense, some one who can crash and torture others scot-free is more greate, then someone who tries to be good and get his ass-kicked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T02:16:47-08:00","id":1475210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475196#post1475196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I never read it as he, personally and alone (except for kinfolk sorcerer aid) did fight the Antedeluvian, but that the attack was a coordinated one, with other garou and other fera, mummies and sorcerers taking part...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fighting an elder (or more) vampire always means more than personal and alone. You need to use own background(Resource/Contact/Allies, etc) to battle him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113",