</div> </div>Well... another proof that Garou are shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T03:28:40-08:00","id":1475214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475212#post1475212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add another canonical one, Vladimir Rustovich, 6th Tzimisce, one of the greatest Voivodes of Transylvanian history and a legendary enemy of the Shadow Lords. To kill him Shadow Lord Evelyn Constantine and her sept called several favors and lost six elders. Also not alone but may have some reference</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... another proof that Garou are shit.<br /> And that's why to serve aWyrm is the only adequaete option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T03:28:48-08:00","id":1475215,"title":"","content":"What males elder Vampires so dangerous is not even their power per se - at least not in terms of their Disciplines, but that is definitely the cream on top.<br /> What makes them so dangerous is the fact that they managed to get so old in the first place.<br /> <br /> They managed to survive hundreds of years in a world where for at least half of the day going outside means instant death.<br /> They managed to survive in centuries during which only being seen at night and not partaking in the everyday of a community not only raised big red flags, but essentially barred you from getting far in any aspect of 'life', unless you are very clever, subtle, opportunistic and good at planning far ahead.<br /> They managed to survive for centuries in times where rival vampires had it much much easier to dispatch of them. Much more feudal, no surveillance, no constant communications, far distances to travel at a much slower pace to even get a cry for help anywhere. *And* travel being much much more dangerous between cities.<br /> They managed to survive while being the playthings of even more elder vampire's wars.<br /> <br /> <br /> Despite all those overwhelming odds, those elder vamps managed to survive, they managed to gain influence and allies. *And* they now have their Disciplines on top, grown over all that time.<br /> <br /> STs who don't play elder vampires as the most paranoid, cunning, clever and resourceful beings on the planet are doing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-22-2022, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T03:38:40-08:00","id":1475217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475215#post1475215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What males elder Vampires so dangerous is not even their power per se - at least not in terms of their Disciplines, but that is definitely the cream on top.<br /> What makes them so dangerous is the fact that they managed to get so old in the first place.<br /> <br /> They managed to survive hundreds of years in a world where for at least half of the day going outside means instant death.<br /> They managed to survive in centuries during which only being seen at night and not partaking in the everyday of a community not only raised big red flags, but essentially barred you from getting far in any aspect of 'life', unless you are very clever, subtle, opportunistic and good at planning far ahead.<br /> They managed to survive for centuries in times where rival vampires had it much much easier to dispatch of them. Much more feudal, no surveillance, no constant communications, far distances to travel at a much slower pace to even get a cry for help anywhere. *And* travel being much much more dangerous between cities.<br /> They managed to survive while being the playthings of even more elder vampire's wars.<br /> <br /> <br /> Despite all those overwhelming odds, those elder vamps managed to survive, they managed to gain influence and allies. *And* they now have their Disciplines on top, grown over all that time.<br /> <br /> STs who don't play elder vampires as the most paranoid, cunning, clever and resourceful beings on the planet are doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they are perfect creatures. Mages, demons and changellings also can evolve in something epic. Only Garou can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T03:41:46-08:00","id":1475218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475213#post1475213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... another proof that Garou are shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? A 6th generation vampire can reach 7 dots in attributes and abilities, even without Disciplines. And while Garou NPCs rarely have Gifts outside their breed, tribe and auspice, certain disciplines are all over the place for old vampires. With 7 Potence and 7 Strength one punch may send even an Elder in Crinos to the floor. And then there are the war ghouls which are a match for a crinos in their own right.<br /> <br /> Sure, doesn't take into account why the garou wouldn't send a party through the penumbra. Have one member peek out to lead the way, while being protected by the rest of the group. Then again, attacking through the penumbra by day wasn't that easy in 2nd Edition, when the penumbra was dark by day and roaming with banes. A thing that radically changed with revised edition, without any metaplot to it, just a retcon...<br /> <br /> The vampire has retainers and allies, too.<br /> And if he is a Dark Age Tzimisce ruler, a fortress to boot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T03:47:02-08:00","id":1475219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475217#post1475217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they are perfect creatures. Mages, demons and changellings also can evolve in something epic. Only Garou can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Margrave might have killed a Nexus Crawler single handedly.<br /> <br /> Just because there aren't any novels or short stories about garou doing epic fights with vampires, doesn't mean they aren't epic in their deeds.<br /> <br /> We already established, that vampires usually deal with werewolves by avoiding any confrontation. If they didn't they would be dead(er). So, there just istn't much of an epic in fighting a vampire. Nexus Crawler on the other hand...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T04:17:08-08:00","id":1475220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475219#post1475219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Margrave might have killed a Nexus Crawler single handedly.<br /> <br /> Just because there aren't any novels or short stories about garou doing epic fights with vampires, doesn't mean they aren't epic in their deeds.<br /> <br /> We already established, that vampires usually deal with werewolves by avoiding any confrontation. If they didn't they would be dead(er). So, there just istn't much of an epic in fighting a vampire. Nexus Crawler on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>But he didn't kill any vampore elders, not to say Melthusih.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T04:29:55-08:00","id":1475221,"title":"","content":"Another one, not garou though, legendary simba Sakhmet directly called upon Sun from Umbra and shined Egypt a week, killing many vampires including 4th setite Scorpion King<br /> <br /> Just in my opinion, in WoD metaplot they may have killed more great elders, but 1) authors don\u2019t have chances to introduce this. 2) both sides simply forget these shit. After all their greatest enemy is Wyrm and their stuff is more focused on that (Talons of Wyrm, Maeljin, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T04:38:48-08:00","id":1475222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475221#post1475221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one, not garou though, legendary simba Sakhmet directly called upon Sun from Umbra and shined Egypt a week, killing many vampires including 4th setite Scorpion King<br /> <br /> Just in my opinion, in WoD metaplot they may have killed more great elders, but 1) authors don\u2019t have chances to introduce this. 2) both sides simply forget these shit. After all their greatest enemy is Wyrm and their stuff is more focused on that (Talons of Wyrm, Maeljin, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet authors recal these shit pretty fast when they need to shit on Garou (like in London with Mithra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 02-22-2022, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T10:17:21-08:00","id":1475242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475215#post1475215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">STs who don't play elder vampires as the most paranoid, cunning, clever and resourceful beings on the planet are doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages would like a word with this assumption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T11:30:36-08:00","id":1475247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475242#post1475242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Archmages would like a word with this assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages tend to not live on the planet, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T12:11:17-08:00","id":1475248,"title":"","content":"Great thing about being an Archmage? Baring the Avatar Storm era, you can exist on the planet and not at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T15:00:33-08:00","id":1475257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475206#post1475206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that's toiching approach... Tbh, I mean Ramsay is better character exactly couse of all the lives he ruined and all the evil he bring.... like someone who FORCED the world remember him. Although book!Ramsey's much dumber and less charismatic. Book!Euron, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> As for gamelines... well looking at large scale it means that vamps are way more awesome kind, than inferior Garou, becouse they can evolve into monsters no Garou hero can match, nevermind how epic he is. Again, cudos for CofD sinse elder werewolves had a (a vague) chance to evolve into something more epic. I just don't care about morality) &quot;Good, bad, I'm the guy with a gun&quot;))<br /> Hense, some one who can crash and torture others scot-free is more greate, then someone who tries to be good and get his ass-kicked.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your fundamental problem is with the fact that Garou do not have the same maximum potential for violence and destruction as other splats like Vampires or Mages, then yeah, that's kind of just the way it is. But you are ignoring the other side of the coin, that your average Garou can probably turn 9 out of 10 Vampires into sausage if they just happen to run into each other on the street. Garou aren't shit, it's just that the most extreme examples of Mages and Vampires are like diamonds. And the vast majority of either splat will *never* get there.<br /> <br /> The really low Generation that turns a Vampire into an overwhelming force-of-nature is a) the product of a &quot;&quot;birth&quot;&quot;-lottery, being lucky enough to have been sired by an Antediluvian or a Methuselah, or b) a long process of gradually eating your way up the food-chain without being murdered by the vastly more powerful beings threatened by your ambition, which also comes with the chance of becoming possessed by one of the rivals you tried to diablerize. And either one of those options requires *centuries* of struggle in order to hone the powers necessary to achieve that potential. While forum-chatter can make it sound like diablerizing your way from a humble 11th Generation all the way up to 4th Generation is just part of regular Vampire gameplay, it really *isn't.* Most Vampires are just struggling to make it from night to night, and will never rise in power to the extent that they can't be swatted out of existence by one of their elders, or a Joe Average Werewolf they have the misfortune of stumbling across in a dark alley.<br /> <br /> (PS: to bring in an earlier example, Vladimir Rustovich was over One Thousand Years Old. There are probably Maeljin Incarna that weren't even born yet when Vladimir was fighting his way up the ranks. And Vladimir is an example of a Vampire committed to being a *warrior*, more than a socialite or scholar.)<br /> <br /> You could probably write a story about a Garou that achieves incredible power through decades of struggle, by forming pacts with powerful spirits, acquiring potent artifacts, pushing themselves to the absolute limit of their potential. And a Werewolf that could continue that process for *centuries* likely would be able to rival the might of a powerful Methuselah. There are just lots of reasons that story doesn't get told, in particular because the themes and setting of WtA aren't meant to encourage that kind of tale. And conversely, almost any Vampire that attempted such a thing would be as likely to die in the attempt as the Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, a Garou could theoretically be empowered by an entity other than the Wyrm. I could be wrong, but I believe that it's theoretically possible for a Garou to become a Kami, though there are reasons why it pretty much never happens. You might argue that a Vampire doesn't need to get its extra power from something else, except yes they do: another Vampire. It's just a question of whether you're being empowered by a Celestine or an Antediluvian, both of which are effectively god-like beings.<br /> <br /> I mean, if it makes you feel better, I'd be inclined to think most Celestines would be able to squash an Antediluvian, if you somehow ended up in the weird situation where they were throwing down with each other in a dark alley. VtM is just kind of unique among the gamelines that it is written with other Vampires as the Biggest Bads in their fish-pond, whereas the Bigger Fish in other gamelines tend to be bigger than a super-charged member of the same splat; Mage comes close, but I think even Archmages are not a proper match for the greatest of the Celestines, but I could be wrong there.<br /> <br /> But to return to the first point, if the thing that interests you most is being able to crush your enemies, then you want to play Vampire: the Masquerade, not Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Specifically, you want to play as a member of the Sabbat. Werewolves don't get to become nigh-unstoppable demigods because their entire story is about fighting a war that's nearly impossible to win, and maybe even that trying to &quot;fight&quot; it in the traditional sense is itself a losing strategy. And yeah, if the only thing you prioritize is a capacity for destruction, then of course the incarnation of cosmic destruction itself is going to be the most likely source of the power that you're seeking. If Ramsay is a better character because he's better at hurting people, then of course the God of Hurting People is the one who is going to help make your Werewolf character &quot;better.&quot; And if you really want to tell that tale in Werewolf, it'll probably be the story of some asshole Garou supplanting Hellbringer as the new Maeljin of Violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 02-22-2022, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T17:05:10-08:00","id":1475273,"title":"","content":"Part of this is survivorship bias. There's no reason for the games to tell us what Methusaleh level vampires were destroyed in the past by Garou. Vampire books tell us about the vampires that survived and exist in the current day. And Werewolf books are mainly concerned about current threats that are hooks for the PCs, not historical battles that are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> So we know of Methusalehs like the All High, Baba Yaga, and Mithras because they survived until the modern nights. But we wouldn't be told for example that the Nosferatu Methusaleh vampire eating children in the Black Forest were destroyed by the Get of Fenris sibling warriors Hansel and Gretl, or that the Fianna destroyed the Malkavian Methusaleh Sirona (the name of a Celtic goddess) in Gaul around the time of Caesar because that would simply be trivia not relevant to the needs of a current sourcebook. But as fictitious examples, they don't serve your needs. But clearly, all those ancient vampires that were once embraced but didn't survive couldn't all have fallen simply to the intrigues of other vampires.<br /> <br /> We do have one canonical example of Garou destroying a ton of vampires - Under a Blood Red Moon. Now none of them are the level of a Methusaleh, but it did include some old vampires and those of more potent blood than is allowed in character creation. Here's the canonical list of casualties in Chicago By Night, Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Neil Graham (9th generation, 60 year Neonate)<br /> Hank Cave (10th generation, 29 year Neonate)<br /> Theodore Dooley (11th generation, 25 year Neonate)<br /> Marc Levesque (9th generation, 123 year Ancilla)<br /> Travis Fett (13th generation, 23 year Neonate)<br /> Gordon Keaton (10th generation, 21 year Neonate)<br /> Priscilla Gibbs (11th generation, 20 year Neonate)<br /> Derrick Stack (9th generation, 11 year Neonate)<br /> Jimmy Holcomb (9th generation, Fledgling)<br /> Jackie Goodman (9th generation, 28 year Neonate, assistant to Archon)<br /> Paula Smith (8th generation, 23 year Neonate)<br /> Ben Smith (8th generation, 23 year Neonate)<br /> Horace Turnball (10th generation, 235 year Elder)<br /> Johann Weltmann (7th generation, 33 year Neonate)<br /> Elizbieta Jurofsky (7th generation, 104 year Ancilla)<br /> Jurgis Rudkus (7th generation, 83 year Neonate)<br /> Peter Walenski (7th generation, 43 year Neonate)<br /> Tommy Walker (9th generation, 29 year Neonate)<br /> Sophia Ayres (7th generation, 12 year Neonate)<br /> Sharon Payne (7th generation, 64 year Neonate)<br /> Michael Payne (8th generation, 64 year Neonate)<br /> Sir Henry Johnson (10th generation, 135 year Ancilla)<br /> Tamoszius Kusleika (9th generation, 108 year Ancilla)<br /> Garwood Marshall (8th generation, 56 year Neonate)<br /> Lodin (7th generation, 141 year Ancilla, Prince)<br /> Tommy Hinds (8th generation, 87 year Neonate)<br /> Edgar Drummond (8th generation, 127 year Ancilla)<br /> Lawrence Ballard (9th generation, 54 year Neonate)<br /> Frank Gaughan (9th generation, 41 year Neonate)<br /> Pham Hong (9th generation, 15 year Neonate)<br /> Bernnon Thornhill (8th generation, 8 year Neonate)<br /> <br /> To these we can additional unnamed vampires destroyed in Under a Blood Red Moon, and at least dozens of ghouls (at least 60, maybe over a 100). In addition, we can assume the Garou who attacked Chicago also defeated many of the other foes present. This includes the Sabbat (a circle of 5 Blood Brothers, 5 scouts, a Nomad Pack, and many new Fledglings \u2013 fate unknown, presumed destroyed; they aren't mentioned in CbN 2e), 1 Abomination (presumed destroyed), and at least 26 Black Spiral Dancers (mentioned as slain in UBRM) plus however many Banes and fomori at the same time. And all of this happened in addition fighting lots of other vampires who somehow managed to escape (we know Abraham DuSable was attacked and survived only by chance). The Garou took losses, but achieved all of their major objectives in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T19:30:30-08:00","id":1475283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475242#post1475242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmages would like a word with this assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they Elder Vampires minus blood already? I don't see your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475273#post1475273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou took losses, but achieved all of their major objectives in canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou literally shape vampire society with their mere presence. There are no such a thing as &quot;Garou-Vampire competition for territory&quot; most of the time, there is just &quot;Domain was abandoned due to reports of Lupines nearby&quot;. And the reason it doesn't happen like that in other splats is just because Garou do not see them as Wyrm-things necessarily.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, part of the problem is more that the authors give the Garou too much credit instead of too little, to the point that they don't write much about them winning because that's kind of assumed once they enter the field (that's part of the Worf Effect).<br /> <br /> Here's the whole point with a Worf Effect: while it may make the character look weak because of taking regular beatings, it isn't born out of the author thinking the character is weak, but that the character is too strong. It is essentially the overuse of a gimmick whose basis is the actual recognition of their overwhelming strength (that the author may admire or despise, but that's another story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T21:32:13-08:00","id":1475294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475283#post1475283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't they Elder Vampires minus blood already? I don't see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages have power far more in-line with the Methuselahs, and their conflicts are even more far reaching. Voormas and Senex are fighting a war over the very existence of the concept of death. Mages are already prone to needing to being clever, cunning, and resourceful because of the nature of their powers. The ones that last centuries and get into the 6+ Sphere territories also have a great deal of paranoia to survive the enemies they amass.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T08:07:36-08:00","id":1475321,"title":"","content":"I think territorial conflict between vampires and werewolves is not necessarily about land. For garou hunt game or simply go to the supermarket. Vampires need blood. There is no conflict there. But, vampires often try to gain influence within the mortal society, which might bring them into conflict with garou kinfolk and by extension the garou. And, those vampires older and wiser, might correctly realise that once the garou are on the trail of one of the vampires, it might be a good thing to lay low for a couple of years...<br /> <br /> That said, the garou should see vampires as wyrm-creatures all of the time, certain post-1st-edition materials tell us - but, still they are the lesser evil in most urban settings, for fomori and banes are possibly more common and more in line with the tenet to &quot;Fight the Wyrm where it dwells and breeds&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wewaupet is basically the only immortal garou - or is he an immortal being that originally was a garou - in any case, we can assume that he is able to kill vampires, if he ever wanted to....<br /> <br /> Besides that, a Legendary Garou can learn the 2nd Edition Player's Guide Gift &quot;Renew the Cycle&quot; and enter into a contested Gosis vs. Willpower roll (difficulty 8 on both sides). If the Garou wins ans pays three permanent Gnosis the Undead is destroyed. This would include Antediluvians or Caine himself. Since an avatar of Helios or Gaia could teach this Gift, one would assume that similar abilities can used by such avatars directly, too - so the Rite of Summoning might bring an adequate result, too, possibly (I generally don't allow to circumvent Rank limitations by summoning a spirit and appeal to him to grant an ability once).<br /> The Gift doesn't cancel the Spell of Life, though: Mummies just die, to be reborn later (pre-Web-of-Faith, that is).<br /> <br /> So, as far as the comparison between rank 6 Garou and Elders go, the Silver Fangs have one specific Gift that might just kill any vampire. In addition to &quot;Mind Block&quot; as an adequate defence against vampire mental abilities...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:04:26-08:00","id":1475342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475321#post1475321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think territorial conflict between vampires and werewolves is not necessarily about land. For garou hunt game or simply go to the supermarket. Vampires need blood. There is no conflict there. But, vampires often try to gain influence within the mortal society, which might bring them into conflict with garou kinfolk and by extension the garou. And, those vampires older and wiser, might correctly realise that once the garou are on the trail of one of the vampires, it might be a good thing to lay low for a couple of years...<br /> <br /> That said, the garou should see vampires as wyrm-creatures all of the time, certain post-1st-edition materials tell us - but, still they are the lesser evil in most urban settings, for fomori and banes are possibly more common and more in line with the tenet to &quot;Fight the Wyrm where it dwells and breeds&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wewaupet is basically the only immortal garou - or is he an immortal being that originally was a garou - in any case, we can assume that he is able to kill vampires, if he ever wanted to....<br /> <br /> Besides that, a Legendary Garou can learn the 2nd Edition Player's Guide Gift &quot;Renew the Cycle&quot; and enter into a contested Gosis vs. Willpower roll (difficulty 8 on both sides). If the Garou wins ans pays three permanent Gnosis the Undead is destroyed. This would include Antediluvians or Caine himself. Since an avatar of Helios or Gaia could teach this Gift, one would assume that similar abilities can used by such avatars directly, too - so the Rite of Summoning might bring an adequate result, too, possibly (I generally don't allow to circumvent Rank limitations by summoning a spirit and appeal to him to grant an ability once).<br /> The Gift doesn't cancel the Spell of Life, though: Mummies just die, to be reborn later (pre-Web-of-Faith, that is).<br /> <br /> So, as far as the comparison between rank 6 Garou and Elders go, the Silver Fangs have one specific Gift that might just kill any vampire. In addition to &quot;Mind Block&quot; as an adequate defence against vampire mental abilities...</div> </div> </div> </div>But you forgot the most powerful discipline held by the antediluvians and Cain, the discipline of 'lol plot armor so screw you and your auto destruction power'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:37:23-08:00","id":1475347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475342#post1475342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you forgot the most powerful discipline held by the antediluvians and Cain, the discipline of 'lol plot armor so screw you and your auto destruction power'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, if I would ever have antediluvians, or caine, in a werewolf chronicle, or a Silver Fang Rank 6 for that matter, I would grant the player the satisfaction to use the power....<br /> <br /> So, look what good it did Ravnos having plot armor and Fortitude, when the plot was against him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Come to think of it, the whole thing with methusalah level vampires and rank 6 garou is the 'Masquerade of the Red Death' problem. The story is okay-ish and the epilogue makes it a perfect VtM-story, but all the characters are totally removed from what is &quot;normal&quot; within the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 02-23-2022, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T16:36:54-08:00","id":1475372,"title":"","content":"Ravnos got taken out by a process that was bit more involved then 'I cast destroy undead, time to save or die scrub' &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T16:41:58-08:00","id":1475373,"title":"","content":"Vampire vs. Werewolf fights are going to be very sus until V:tM drops its standing &quot;Character Rank = Discipline level&quot; crossover rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T17:06:21-08:00","id":1475376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475373#post1475373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire vs. Werewolf fights are going to be very sus until V:tM drops its standing &quot;Character Rank = Discipline level&quot; crossover rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree weren't for the fact that this works fine(ish) with every other splat.<br /> <br /> The specific problem here is the rules for Gifts that are really, really obnoxious. Werewolves have the worse supernatural start of all splats, everyone else can start at 3 just fine and most can increase to 5 with Freebies, or with less effort to increase than Werewolves increasing Rank to 4 anyway. Werewolves need a thorough revision of the Gift system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T21:50:20-08:00","id":1475393,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;compare power level&quot; works particular well at all. Mages, for example, do most of their bread and butter stuff at 1-3 dots. 4+ Sphere effects are rarely cast in the middle of things, as they're difficulty goes up and usually deal with much broader scope effects. What really defines a mage's power in most supernatural show downs is how many Spheres they have a few dots in rather than having them at high ratings.<br /> <br /> Likewise a changeling's ability to use Glamour to cheat Realm requirements, or just flat out use Unleashing, makes the 1-5 dot ratings of Arts a very poor fit for that model.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, it's not actually a rule. It's a suggestion for handling crossover.<br /> <br /> I also don't think Garou start that bad just because they start at Rank 1. The Gifts aren't 1-5 powers, and plenty of the Rank 1 and 2 Gifts will be useful for entire campaigns, while many of the high level ones might be really good when they're useful, but niche enough to only be used a handful of times even in a very long game. The Garou also have one of the strongest set of innate abilities of the splats. Persuasion is a Rank 1 Gift, but easily one of the best social powers in the whole WoD (if very ST interpretation dependent), it's only weak if you use the whole compare ratings thing as an attempt to equalize the crossover playing field because it's a Rank 1 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T23:51:45-08:00","id":1475396,"title":"","content":"I think for crossover direct powers comparison, all Gifts of an Athro are considered 4th level Gifts, regardless of the level the Gift was learned on. Also, some Gifts like Mind Block are absolute. It is level 4, iirc, but I wouldn't even Dominate 8 bypass it, for it is meant to be absolute.<br /> <br /> Then, direct comparison, of which power is blocking which other power is rarely needed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T05:31:57-08:00","id":1475401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475393#post1475393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;compare power level&quot; works particular well at all. Mages, for example, do most of their bread and butter stuff at 1-3 dots. 4+ Sphere effects are rarely cast in the middle of things, as they're difficulty goes up and usually deal with much broader scope effects. What really defines a mage's power in most supernatural show downs is how many Spheres they have a few dots in rather than having them at high ratings.<br /> <br /> Likewise a changeling's ability to use Glamour to cheat Realm requirements, or just flat out use Unleashing, makes the 1-5 dot ratings of Arts a very poor fit for that model.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, it's not actually a rule. It's a suggestion for handling crossover.<br /> <br /> I also don't think Garou start that bad just because they start at Rank 1. The Gifts aren't 1-5 powers, and plenty of the Rank 1 and 2 Gifts will be useful for entire campaigns, while many of the high level ones might be really good when they're useful, but niche enough to only be used a handful of times even in a very long game. The Garou also have one of the strongest set of innate abilities of the splats. Persuasion is a Rank 1 Gift, but easily one of the best social powers in the whole WoD (if very ST interpretation dependent), it's only weak if you use the whole compare ratings thing as an attempt to equalize the crossover playing field because it's a Rank 1 power.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I read it, it refers more to the level of the user in the power than the level of the effect. The comparison is User's Level in Discipline/Art/Sphere/User's Rank.<br /> <br /> Now, this can't work perfectly because of how the WoD was built, and the &quot;-ish&quot; in my statement is precisely because it is still a poor improvisation, but I think it does a passable job more frequently than not when you need the comparison, and specifically talking about this particular tangent we're in.<br /> <br /> For Changelings Unleashing and Realm bypassing does not change the Art level, which is even still their dice pool (in fact may be their entire dice pool) and measure of control, so I think that Art level is the most fitting of all, more than Disciplines. Mages have an overall trade-off of potency for versatility, as you see on the usual rules for Nightfolk powers in Mage proper. None of those are meant to work as this rule does, but when they come into conflict and their proper rules can't solve it, the comparison works ok as a breaker, until the Rank comes in.<br /> <br /> You're right that Gifts aren't 1-5 powers, but that's part of the problem. They're very inconsistent in power and utility, extremely sensible to mastery of the system even for WoD standards, with two characters with access to the same number of them at the same levels being possibly wildly different in capability to remain relevant in the same game. All the while they're not level powers, but their access and cost works as if they were, specially if the ST doesn't feel comfortable with Spirits giving them &quot;out of the counter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Those are problems with the Gift system regardless of crossover. A better level definition untied from Rank would be a solution. Not the only option, but an option. It so happens that revising the Gift system would also potentially help with the crossover rule of thumb, since as it is now we have the problem that no stand-in for supernatural potency for Shapechangers makes sense other than Rank, that barely do so at all.<br /> <br /> But all that is a tangent on mechanical specifics for crossover games, which is a poor comparison anyway because they're not meant to mechanically communicate. For the thread's actual point I agree with you that the Garou aren't really short on supernatural resources. Gifts aren't only personal powers to begin with, but also, well, gifts. Which reinforces their relationship with the entities that gifted those powers to begin with. Between Gifts, Totems, Fetishes, and generally being in talking terms with freaking gods I'd say they have more than enough supernatural back-up to wreak as much or more havoc than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Mechanical problems also go both ways, as Vampire has the general problem with too few means to control Difficulty directly or not, and general lack of rules on equipment, mundane or supernatural, that makes them more reliant on personal capabilities than it actually makes sense for the setting. And the focus problem of the thread does not rely on those mechanical specifics anyway, it is born out of bad authorial decisions, just not to the proportions some think, give or take the already clear distinction on standards for what constitutes an interesting/good character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T23:56:57-08:00","id":1475437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475222#post1475222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Onyx Pathe essentually assert gamelines at WtA expense. And demote Garou to biggest loosers of WoD, who only exist to be humilated.<br /> See? I don't know why WW hate Garou that much, but it seems the LOVE to humilate them.<br /> Yet authors recal these shit pretty fast when they need to shit on Garou (like in London with Mithra).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what your problem is but this negative attitude isn't helping you or anyone else to have a reasonable discussion<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475182#post1475182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as I said it is cheap storytelling</div> </div> </div> </div>As Monteparnas said, this is the real problem. WoD lore suffers from having a whole bunch of different authors, with different agendas, and, frankly, poor quality work. On top of that the rules are written by a different bunch of people/different approach and have to conform to a system that has well known weaknesses and that often doesn't match the fiction surrounding it, so we end up with a long list of purple prose with rules that don't match, or vice versa (anyone want to start _another_ thread on Nosferatu appearance?).<br /> <br /> However, none of that really matters. The lore is meant to be inspirational, the rules are meant to help you balance players against each other, but you have to take it and make it your own game.<br /> <br /> Having a bad attitude about poor quality fiction in a game doesn't do anyone any good, all it does is kick off fights on forums.<br /> <br /> My advice: don't read _any_ of the WoD fiction but if you have to remember it's there just for inspiration, not to define a reality that you have to adhere to<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T00:16:05-08:00","id":1475438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475437#post1475437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice: don't read _any_ of the WoD fiction but if you have to remember it's there just for inspiration, not to define a reality that you have to adhere to</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am being honest, most WtA fiction cannot even remember the basic ways the game works to be an example of play. Only the tribe novels and Song of the Unmaking actually use the setting as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> To the topic at hand, I personally think that Vampire vs Werewolf conflicts in fiction are stunted to make them stand out. If we went with the way both work in terms of rules/setting, it would resemble vampire vs vampire conflict too much to stand out. Instead, making the werewolves into rageballs that lack the tools vampires have but make it up with sheer power makes them distinct from fighting other vampires.<br /> <br /> This is the same reason why WtA fiction often forgets things like challenges, ranks, the Litany, rites or gifts. Because those would get in the way of a good story. For example, Poison Tree's conflict would have been solved easily by simply using the Litany and challenges.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T01:26:03-08:00","id":1475439,"title":"","content":"It seems very odd to assert that they get in the way of a good story when people have been playing the game for thirty years and been creating great stories using the rules.<br /> <br /> Bending the rules a bit for the fiction is one thing. Tossing out the rules (esp. rules that enforce the actual setting in the first place) makes no sense. If you can't write good fiction pieces while respecting the setting the rules are made to emulate, either (1) you're not trying to write for the game in the first place or (2) the setting isn't good and shouldn't be used for people to craft their own stories in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T02:45:55-08:00","id":1475441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475439#post1475439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems very odd to assert that they get in the way of a good story when people have been playing the game for thirty years and been creating great stories using the rules.<br /> <br /> Bending the rules a bit for the fiction is one thing. Tossing out the rules (esp. rules that enforce the actual setting in the first place) makes no sense. If you can't write good fiction pieces while respecting the setting the rules are made to emulate, either (1) you're not trying to write for the game in the first place or (2) the setting isn't good and shouldn't be used for people to craft their own stories in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree, but I think the issue is that many of the writers hired to do the official novels don't really know the setting well. There are many short stories that have the basic skeleton of the setting, but then lack things like gifts/rites/ranks/Litany.<br /> <br /> I think the issue is that WtA requires deep knowledge of the setting and its culture to write believably. Meanwhile, VtM can be done with only basic knowledge of clans and the basic rules. Kindred/Cainites are still basically typical vampires, Garou are far from typical werewolves. Often, the writers get as far as fighting the wyrm, the tribes, the auspices and MAYBE the breeds.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you aren't familiar with WtA really deeply, writing a good story for it can be extremely hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T03:32:49-08:00","id":1475442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475441#post1475441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly agree, but I think the issue is that many of the writers hired to do the official novels don't really know the setting well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think WW officials bragged about a lot of hidden lore to Robert Weinberg before he wrote &quot;Masquerade of the Red Death&quot; and that this is why the story turned out, like it did.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T03:57:25-08:00","id":1475443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475441#post1475441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mostly agree, but I think the issue is that many of the writers hired to do the official novels don't really know the setting well. There are many short stories that have the basic skeleton of the setting, but then lack things like gifts/rites/ranks/Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really excuse the issue regardless of where the fault may fall. If someone's writing for an existing setting, they should be provided the basics necessary to make sure they're following the core elements of the setting, and they should read said material with the ability to ask questions if any key plot points might need more details.<br /> <br /> We're not talking anything super arduous here. The first ~100 pages of W20 covers almost everything except the specific functions of Gifts and Rites (though enough to know those are things in Garou society). Ranks, the Litany, and challenge-culture, the Auspices/Breeds/Tribes and so on are all in there; if briefly. I know plenty of the fiction we're talking about is from before W20 came out, but we're not talking about needing to spend a week reading to get most of these things down.<br /> <br /> The whole reason there's a concept of a &quot;setting Bible&quot; is because IPs that are going to have multiple teams that might be working independently of each other and the core creative team benefit from an easily digestible document that ensures a base-line of commonality. It doesn't mean you have to have as in depth knowledge as hardcore fans just to write a novel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T04:54:09-08:00","id":1475445,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Yeah, I agree fully. I'm just trying to theorize on the -why- it often is like that with WtA fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T05:06:13-08:00","id":1475446,"title":"","content":"The problem is, that the &quot;setting Bible&quot; seems to haven't been that necessary in the past. Even the line developer changed over the decades and with that a lot of themes and moods of the game. That is for WtA (and Mage) more true, subjectively, than for Vampire, and less obvious in the game lines that didn't get their own core books in revised like Wraith and CtD.<br /> <br /> <br /> For all the Storytelling games the storytelling aspect was always in the foreground, while a consistent setting or rules that are absolute, well defined and work as laws of nature within the setting, were always something of less importance.<br /> <br /> Therefore, some of the 1st Edition novels are a fun read, if you don't think too much about the rules and their application, while others are downright awful...<br /> I mean, Cry to Battle: The author too seems to have been informed about some WtA background and some MtA stuff and then delivered something that just wasn't a good thing within the broader context of the setting(s).<br /> <br /> Then again, even the fluff within the Core rules is sometimes just bad. Revised editions fluff paragraph for the Rituals knowledge trait makes it seem like the Rite of Dedication is an affair that takes mere moments and can be done with moments notice while being on a stake out, when the casual conversation reveals that one garou doesn't wear dedicated cloth. Is that precedence? Should it be?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T06:03:58-08:00","id":1475448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475445#post1475445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Yeah, I agree fully. I'm just trying to theorize on the -why- it often is like that with WtA fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason is simple and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> already cracked it: poor quality writing.<br /> <br /> We love this game and it is easy to imagine the company behind it as extremely professional and prepared, with complex reasons behind all those decisions. But actually WW never was any of that. It is a bunch of semi-amateurs that had a good idea and forwarded it with passion.<br /> <br /> Hiring people either already knowledgeable about the work or informing them adequately is basic. They didn't do it. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>, a consistent setting <b><u>IS</u></b> a storytelling aspect, and an important one, they just have always been used to mistake focus on storytelling to not having to give a shit for details as long as you have fun at the moment.<br /> <br /> Basic mistakes are all over the place, and that's why the fiction is like that: it is simply written by or at the behest of people without any technical training to do what they're doing. Which was good enough, by the way, since they did had good ideas and made an interesting setting, but the lack of technical knowledge shows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T06:26:02-08:00","id":1475451,"title":"","content":"This post is actually strange since if there is a splat in WoD that needs nerf, its definitely werewolves, don't think about the lore too much (as others have pointed out, WW writing was always crappy) because a starting werewolf will easily merk most other splats and most of their gameline enemies in one or two turns, what more could you possibly want from them? Elders are basically demigods while Antediluvians are genuine gods period, none of the other splats (including other vamps themselves) are really supposed to be able to fight them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 02-25-2022, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T13:35:17-08:00","id":1475465,"title":"","content":"The Garou don't need a nerf, at all (and they're not the strongest WoD starting PCs even if it's hard to compare since there's no one edition with all of them in it).<br /> <br /> The Garou have the best starting package in a stand up white room close combat fight. The farther you get away from that hypothetical ideal, the worse their specific starting package gets.<br /> <br /> This is, ultimately, a huge part of the issue. They never get treated as more than their starting package in the fiction: furry blenders of doom that while destroy you in close combat, but are easily defeated by anyone that actually thinks about fighting them in any other way. It's a hilariously high Rank 6 legendary Gift just to force an enemy into a &quot;fair&quot; one-on-one duel, but everything between what a Cub gets, and what a Legend gets, that helps the Garou not get slaughtered by anyone withe a brain is ignored. As well it sells the real combat abilities of lots of the other supernaturals short. Basically, only looking at &quot;Go Crinos and Rage attack until dead&quot; abilities of the Garou does all of the WoD fiction a disservice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T14:50:13-08:00","id":1475468,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Its been a while since I played apocalypse but the &quot;Go Crinos and Rage untill dead&quot; is pretty much how it always worked, aggravated damage and multiple attacks are not something you can really contest, also I would like to know how could a garou get &quot;easily slaughtered&quot; barring their players intentionally walking into a silver meatgrinder, stepping sideways is also a ridiculously big advantage for anything since it allows them to spy and pick on their targets however they please and thats without getting into gifts, the lore might like to use them as punching bags sometimes but the game mechanics are another story entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T16:47:58-08:00","id":1475473,"title":"","content":"&quot;I played some WtA and that's how it went,&quot; doesn't really communicate a lot meaningfully here.<br /> <br /> If using Crinos/Rage and stepping sideways is always an option, that's just playing into the white room hypothetical best case for Garou.<br /> <br /> Thinks that mess with that:<br /> <br /> 1) Long ranged attacks. Remember that, in combat for most Garou, lethal and agg are barely different. Half a dozen ghouls with high powered rifles will drop a Garou fairly easily, and even if the Garou survives the first round, they're going to burn through Rage like mad to close in to close range and then not have lots of extra actions to deal with all the people with guns.<br /> <br /> 2) Silver.<br /> <br /> 3) Fighting in cities: high Gauntlet means no Umbra shenanigans, and lots of cameras/etc. to keep shifting in check.<br /> <br /> 4) Almost no resistances to non-physical supernatural attacks at starting level. Social and mental powers to force Rage and WP spending into the ground.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T17:03:25-08:00","id":1475474,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that the long-ranged attack point is just as much a white room assumption as Crinos and stepping sideways always being an option. Really bare open fields can be difficult to find, and if you're in an urban area, firing rifles off is going to get attention even in Gothic-Punk land. Also, a fair number of urban areas have subways and other subterranean reaches, which are favored transportation routes for Bone Gnawers, the most populous tribe of werewolves. Visibility will be limited, a wolf form can grant access to escape routes that humans might not be able to take, and Ragabash are going to be excitedly rubbing their hands together at the notion of someone coming down to play in their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T21:53:47-08:00","id":1475480,"title":"","content":"I don't see things as strange. Hell I think it's the natural result of these splats and their attitudes.<br /> <br /> Vampires and mages and others are selfish, heaven defying creatures that look to live a long time and beat the natural order. Because they can live a long time, they can find more power.<br /> <br /> Garou and Fera are essentially agents of the world. They follow the will of the heavens, they're trying to right the triat and reach an equilibrium. Culturally they've got this &quot;we're all in this together&quot; attitude so seeking Immortality and ultimate power is a no-no. Garou look for an awesome death, not eternal life, and without a long life they can never reach the power of Vamps, Mages, Demons, Fae and so on. A Garou who saught long life would almost certainly get rejected by garou and the spirits they're overly dependent on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-26-2022, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T21:19:05-08:00","id":1475516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475474#post1475474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that the long-ranged attack point is just as much a white room assumption as Crinos and stepping sideways always being an option. Really bare open fields can be difficult to find, and if you're in an urban area, firing rifles off is going to get attention even in Gothic-Punk land. Also, a fair number of urban areas have subways and other subterranean reaches, which are favored transportation routes for Bone Gnawers, the most populous tribe of werewolves. Visibility will be limited, a wolf form can grant access to escape routes that humans might not be able to take, and Ragabash are going to be excitedly rubbing their hands together at the notion of someone coming down to play in their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's actually the point: get out of the White Room and things are far more complicated, and the Bone Gnawers work precisely because Werewolves <b>aren't</b> just that starting package of damage dealing and regeneration.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have a huge starting advantage on the combat avenue. But that's it. They live and fight in the same WoD as everyone else, so they need to read situations and deal with complex contexts as everyone else. It isn't that they <b>are</b> at risk of being slaughtered by everything else, but that if they <b>were</b> indeed the mindless killing machines of the fiction, they <b>would</b> be at such a risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T22:21:22-08:00","id":1475520,"title":"","content":"You know what the great thing about the Gauntlet is?<br /> <br /> It doesn't interfere with Presence and Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T01:49:45-08:00","id":1475524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475448#post1475448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>, a consistent setting <b><u>IS</u></b> a storytelling aspect...</div> </div> </div> </div>An inconsistent setting is also a storytelling aspect. Enter: Doctor Who.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, the Setting is inconsistent as hell and nobody ever seemed to keep that is check during the first editions. Later, for W20 changing breeds and W20 Rage across the World hat some &quot;open development&quot; and fans contributed some ideas to improve consistency.<br /> <br /> But yeah, story bits and novels are, for a large part, not concerned with the rules, because they tell a story. And how any individual troupe handles adhering to the rules is also quite different, I'd imagine. Because, there are bits and pieces all over the place, and some STs read this and that and extrapolate stuff to - leading to very different interpretations of the game word.<br /> <br /> The light/dark penumbra illumination difference is just one example. That &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; would find pre-change cubs without fail pre revised but could never find them post-W20 - which both are absolute statements that each make a whole bunch of character backgrounds implausible, is another. Not to mention, that there are implications of things that exist with the game world, that aren't put into rules (like W20's fail to re-vamp the Baptism of Fire and its carbon copy of the 'Test tube' talen indicating that there is another way to determine pre-change kids).<br /> And what about an attack. Is a lunge forward part of an claw attack. I mean Crinoses are large and have pretty long arms, right? And Rage actions allow for any physical action, closing in to a an opponent surely should be in the realm of possible actions, right? But W20 (I think shattered dream) made a gift specific for movement with rage actions, implicating that this would normally not be the case. And how long does it take to learn a dot of anything? Is the mechanic provided by the instruction secondary ability the rule that governs the universe in that regard, or not?<br /> <br /> If players and ST have access to different bit or information or even interpret them differently, the game worlds can be quite different. And the same is true for all the novel authors. They all wrote what in their minds is a valid WtA story. Or short story. And partly, they had different amounts of background knowledge to begin with.<br /> <br /> I have the same problem with new players to the LARP, who came into WtA with W20, because our game world is a &quot;everything is true, but tabletop NPCs play a diminished role&quot;-2nd/revised-mixture. So, the game worlds are different. The Rite of Heritage, for example, is for us regarded as somewhat obscure Get Rite (for it stems from their Tribebooks) but W20 put it in the general Rites section. Performing the Rite, for example to verify the identity of guests to the sept, changes social interactions completely.<br /> <br /> So, to enjoy the stories, a certain suspense of disbelief is necessary and the assumption, that they describe, to some degree, one-time events and special snowflake characters, and aren't meant to be depictions of the status quo in the game setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T15:47:00-08:00","id":1475949,"title":"","content":"DA:Werewolf has a sample chronicle in which the BBEG is a 5th gen Gangrel Meth (Arnulf\u2019s sire, Pard). The whole idea behind the scenario is that you gather a pack capable of getting rid of him and save your Caern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 03-07-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:58:04-07:00","id":1477355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475448#post1475448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason is simple and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> already cracked it: <b>poor quality writing.</b><br /> <br /> We love this game and it is easy to imagine the company behind it as extremely professional and prepared, with complex reasons behind all those decisions. But actually WW never was any of that.<b> It is a bunch of semi-amateurs that had a good idea and forwarded it with passion</b>.<br /> <br /> Hiring people either already knowledgeable about the work or informing them adequately is basic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had to post to say this, a thousand times this...<br /> <br /> Most of the issues that I have with the World of Darkness (Gypsies book, KotE and its orientalism, Vampires generations are mathematically inconsistent, Rage as an attribute, the patchouli-hippie-granola mentality about the Traditions, etc) derive from poor quality writing. We, the fanbase, have collectively glorified the setting, but it was full of bad/dumb/insensitive material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T14:28:54-07:00","id":1477362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1475949#post1475949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DA:Werewolf has a sample chronicle in which the BBEG is a 5th gen Gangrel Meth (Arnulf\u2019s sire, Pard). The whole idea behind the scenario is that you gather a pack capable of getting rid of him and save your Caern</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind me another canonical example. DA: British Isles has a 5th gens Lhiannan called Magda (maybe greatest remaining Lhian), who is also the greatest enemy of Irelandish Fianna. \u201c Magda's knowledge of and affinity with the land is such that even the most powerful Garou have been unable to curtail her activities, each effort to do so resulting in bloody carnage.\u201d<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Magda\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Magda</a><br /> <br /> Of course, no her news in modern, maybe she has been destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T17:19:21-07:00","id":1477374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477362#post1477362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remind me another canonical example. DA: British Isles has a 5th gens Lhiannan called Magda (maybe greatest remaining Lhian), who is also the greatest enemy of Irelandish Fianna. \u201c Magda's knowledge of and affinity with the land is such that even the most powerful Garou have been unable to curtail her activities, each effort to do so resulting in bloody carnage.\u201d<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Magda\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Magda</a><br /> <br /> Of course, no her news in modern, maybe she has been destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire clan got exterminated not too long after the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T18:18:40-07:00","id":1477377,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how open conflict between vampires and werewolves is possible. Vampires are completely helpless during the day. Sure, completely hidden elders can very slowly squeeze werewolf territory financially/politically, maybe even arrange the occasional assassination, but an open war over a specific territory with a known vampire enemy? 5th gen or not she should have been casually hunted down and killed by a very minor pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T19:19:23-07:00","id":1477382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477377#post1477377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how open conflict between vampires and werewolves is possible. Vampires are completely helpless during the day. Sure, completely hidden elders can very slowly squeeze werewolf territory financially/politically, maybe even arrange the occasional assassination, but an open war over a specific territory with a known vampire enemy? 5th gen or not she should have been casually hunted down and killed by a very minor pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <i>Rite of the Questing Stone</i> during day hours + Crinos form upon a torpid vampire = Pile of ashes.<br /> <br /> You can say that ghouls and servitors (Vohzd and similar) protect the vampire, but still, most things will die to a starting pack. Werewolves are built to fight abominations on steroids, ghouls are no match.<br /> <br /> I even <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">made an starting character</a> that on its own can kill nearly every stated Vampire on the books, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack#post1436799\">a starting level pack</a> that can face nearly everything.<br /> <br /> Again, these are not Rank 6 Garou with tons of experience points, just some min-maxing with purely starting stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-25-2022, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T01:34:03-07:00","id":1477415,"title":"","content":"I think there's always been a disconnect between what the authors think an experience Garou's sheet looks like and what a Garou with an experience player behind the wheel and a bunch of XP looks like. Sure, to an extent, all of the games have NPCs stated without too much thought about optimization and what not, but WtA tends to be the absolute worse (a lot of this is that Gifts are dirt cheap, and things that not Garou that have a chance to buy, in or out of splat, should ever pass on are constantly skipped probably because the Gift lists with all the supplements are so huge).<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure if I I could make a 300 XP Adren PC that could easily whoop any stated Garou in a one-on-one fight. It doesn't even require some sort of crazy min-maxing.<br /> <br /> Though things like how easy it is to get Fetishes is always a bit tricky. Monkey Puzzles are a huge game changer, and their level 4 value recognizes that, but that means most Septs have at least one around and you really don't need a lot of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T07:00:29-07:00","id":1477439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477415#post1477415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA tends to be the absolute worse (a lot of this is that Gifts are dirt cheap, and things that not Garou that have a chance to buy, in or out of splat, should ever pass on are constantly skipped probably because the Gift lists with all the supplements are so huge).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I am tired of seeing Ahroun's without <i>Spirit of the Fra</i>y (who doesn't take this?) or Garou in general missing <i>Sense Wyrm</i> (so you are saying you dont have a cheap way to detect your main enemy?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T10:15:09-07:00","id":1477451,"title":"","content":"Well, you are right but....<br /> .... there is a difference between what a player would buy for an optimized character and what a character should or shouldn't have in the mind of the author who came up with the characters backstory.<br /> <br /> Have you ever joined a mid-level D&amp;D/Pathfinder game? If you use the wealth per level rules your magic items will be tailored to you characters abilities. A character who is played up to mid-level will still have the items found as loot or that were available during the campaign. But if the group was in areas with small settlements and didn't have time to craft stuff themselves these items will never be as neatly augmenting the characters abilities as if they were hand-picked from scratch.<br /> <br /> That is why I think the authors possibly do not put to much thought into optimizing any NPC but interpolate their traits mainly from what they think their experiences have been...<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> There is a discussion in out LARP game, every now and then, about &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot;. There is a reason why it is a Theurge gift, and if you do not get it by breed and tribe you probably shouldn't use it. <i>Sense Wyrm is not Detect Evil </i>and similar information indicate that you should have the dicepool and understanding to use the gift. For, it does detect wyrm taint and not the garou's main enemy, exclusively.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Unless a fetish is tied to a sept office or something similar I don't think fetishes should be shared among the garou. There is a roll to attune to a fetish and, although not explicitly stated, I would believe that this cuts the ties to the previous owner, therefore it would require a constant re-attuning of the fetish to share it. And while some fetishes might allow that or use alternate rules, because it makes sense, fetishes in general should not be shared among the septmates...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-26-2022, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:07:11-07:00","id":1477460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477377#post1477377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how open conflict between vampires and werewolves is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are manipulators and infiltrators first and foremost. Garou, despite all their directness in comparison to <i>other splats</i>, are masters of <b><u>guerrilla warfare</u></b>, not of open field army clashing.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that open conflict means both already failed and only lasts while they're retreating. They equally loath the idea of enemies learning anything that makes them able to locate and attack their homes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477382#post1477382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I even <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">made an starting character</a> that on its own can kill nearly every stated Vampire on the books, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack#post1436799\">a starting level pack</a> that can face nearly everything.<br /> <br /> Again, these are not Rank 6 Garou with tons of experience points, just some min-maxing with purely starting stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which says absolutely nothing on how things should be on the books or fiction.<br /> <br /> In absolutely any RPG there's a huge difference between what a player can do and what the NPCs should look like, specially what should be the default among them. PCs are special by definition and have access to things based on game balance and game needs for special characters. NPCs are story elements, and standard NPCs are setting elements.<br /> <br /> <b>You</b> have access to just pick and chose what Gifts you have, what Fetishes you have, what Totem you have. The same as <b>you</b> chose Tribe and Auspice for your character. In-setting, things aren't like that and have nothing to do with how hard or easy something is for player to pick.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said Apocalypse is particularly guilty of having particularly disparate pieces to build a character upon, which increasingly widens the gap between what you can do when optimizing a character and what your average NPC looks like, but the principle still holds.<br /> <br /> So, while you can build such characters and they're perfectly valid, as a setting premise they're probably exceedingly rare, unique or currently non-existent. While you may decide every character you build has <i>Sense the Wyrm</i> because it is useful, not even most Theurges or Silver Fangs will have it, you can barely guarantee every sept has <b>one</b> member with it (although most probably do). The same goes for rites and fetishes, you can have them all available for PCs, no problem, and always chose your preferred ones for your characters, that's nice. But the idea that the NPCs have the same access level just doesn't work like that, isn't the settings premise and would make for a rather bland game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:31:20-07:00","id":1477466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477451#post1477451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you are right but....<br /> .... there is a difference between what a player would buy for an optimized character and what a character should or shouldn't have in the mind of the author who came up with the characters backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it isn't even &quot;optimized.&quot; There's a bunch of no-brainer level 1 to 3 Gifts - many of which are core book ones at that - which make no sense for an Elder to have just skipped. I mean, Rite of the Questing Stone was mentioned, but what about Pulse of the Prey (formerly Sense of the Prey)? What Fostern Ragabash would seriously give up on what's probably the best tracking power for the cost in the entire cWoD (It's just 6XP)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever joined a mid-level D&amp;D/Pathfinder game? If you use the wealth per level rules your magic items will be tailored to you characters abilities. A character who is played up to mid-level will still have the items found as loot or that were available during the campaign. But if the group was in areas with small settlements and didn't have time to craft stuff themselves these items will never be as neatly augmenting the characters abilities as if they were hand-picked from scratch. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, IME, WtA is the opposite when it comes to what played PCs look like to what experienced stated NPCs look like. There's a number of reasons for this, but especially since gaining Backgrounds, Renown, Rank, and Rites are all things that take in-play actions without having dedicated XP costs, and don't have the &quot;size of town and what's available in them&quot; issue thanks to Septs and Moonbridges, playing from start generally gets you way more than coming in with mid-game with some extra dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a discussion in out LARP game, every now and then, about &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot;. There is a reason why it is a Theurge gift, and if you do not get it by breed and tribe you probably shouldn't use it. </div> </div> </div>Sense Wyrm is in-splat for one Breed, one Auspice, and <b>five</b> living Tribes. It's the most commonly accessible Gift in the game (131/190 possible combinations of Breed/Auspice/Tribe get you Sense Wyrm as in-splat at least once). If you have it despite that, why shouldn't you use it? Perception and Occult are not exclusively useful to any splat. Like a lot of sensory powers, the more people that have it and roll it the better, because it increases the odds of a good roll by one of them; even if not the statistically best suited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Sense Wyrm is not Detect Evil </i>and similar information indicate that you should have the dicepool and understanding to use the gift. For, it does detect wyrm taint and not the garou's main enemy, exclusively. </div> </div> </div>Sense Wyrm isn't perfect, but still incredibly useful. Obviously like any rolled Gift having dice is good (but as noted it's not a hard pool for Garou to justify), and &quot;understanding&quot; is imparted as part of the learning process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless a fetish is tied to a sept office or something similar I don't think fetishes should be shared among the garou. </div> </div> </div>The idea that Septs have a store of Talens and Fetishes that are given on a temporary basis is in the books. Lots of Fetishes are situational in their applications, and are best kept communally and attuned for an in-depth mission before being returned, rather than held by one Garou that might not need it lots of the time they have it. Monkey Puzzles are a perfect example of the kind of Fetish that makes sense to share. As a rank 4 Fetish it's not common, and most Garou don't need it's effects frequently, so the Sept is better having one or two they can assign to a pack when needed.<br /> <br /> Yes, you lose the attunement, but that's sort of the point. It's not &quot;yours&quot; it's something being entrusted to you for your mission to the Sept's cause.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T12:43:32-07:00","id":1477468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477460#post1477460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NPCs are story elements, and standard NPCs are setting elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that stated NPCs are also gaming elements. NPCs with stats that don't make sense for their stated role in the setting are a reduction in value as elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, while you can build such characters and they're perfectly valid, as a setting premise they're probably exceedingly rare, unique or currently non-existent. </div> </div> </div>Why? The linked example might be pushing into &quot;unusual&quot; but very little there is presented in the books as rare.<br /> <br /> That's kinda the problem here. We're not talking about rare Gifts that you need to find special spirits to learn, or join secret camps to know about. We're not talking about Fetishes only the greatest craftspeople among the Garou can make. A lot of these things are presented, in the books, as things where most packs will have at least one, not &quot;maybe one in the whole Sept.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the idea that the NPCs have the same access level just doesn't work like that, isn't the settings premise and would make for a rather bland game. </div> </div> </div>It is the setting premise though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T13:05:24-07:00","id":1477469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, it isn't even &quot;optimized.&quot; There's a bunch of no-brainer level 1 to 3 Gifts - many of which are core book ones at that - which make no sense for an Elder to have just skipped. I mean, Rite of the Questing Stone was mentioned, but what about Pulse of the Prey (formerly Sense of the Prey)? What Fostern Ragabash would seriously give up on what's probably the best tracking power for the cost in the entire cWoD (It's just 6XP)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even level 1 Gifts must be taught by specific spirits. While you may say that those aren't really that specific or hard to find, this is still enough for not every high-ranking Garou to have had the opportunity at the right point in time. Similarly with Fetishes and Rites.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree that high-ranking Garou are far more likely to have learned such Gifts. That was not what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> was saying, though, and doesn't means specific characters should have learned them either. Or even that the sheets for experienced characters should be read as exhausting for lists of powers/fetishes instead of examples. No such list should be taken as exhausting in a game with so many published Gifts throughout so many books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, IME, WtA is the opposite when it comes to what played PCs look like to what experienced stated NPCs look like. There's a number of reasons for this, but especially since gaining Backgrounds, Renown, Rank, and Rites are all things that take in-play actions without having dedicated XP costs, and don't have the &quot;size of town and what's available in them&quot; issue thanks to Septs and Moonbridges, playing from start generally gets you way more than coming in with mid-game with some extra dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes a lot of difference, but doesn't eliminates the core argument that reaching a given point in the game with whatever the game threw at you is far different from being able to pick and choose what you'll have from the lists in the books, freely. And even for in-game searches the PC's have the advantage of the players knowing such lists, so they have far more intimacy with the idea and the process than the characters, specially the NPCs, necessarily would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sense Wyrm is in-splat for one Breed, one Auspice, and <b>five</b> living Tribes. It's the most commonly accessible Gift in the game (131/190 possible combinations of Breed/Auspice/Tribe get you Sense Wyrm as in-splat at least once). If you have it despite that, why shouldn't you use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it being in-splat doesn't mean it being what you got to pick. Is it common? Sure is. But any given Cliath is more likely than not to <b>not</b> have any particular Gift, as the list of options is still far greater than the number of picks and their actual circumstances and knowledge at the time are very limited.<br /> <br /> After that, again, it depends a lot. Some won't have the opportunity at a convenient time, some won't want for whatever personal reason, and some will simply be so bad at it that they don't pick or pick and don't use. Some may be wary of picking it because tales of bad uses with ugly results are a thing and they don't feel confident. Some achieve to aggravate the spirits that could teach them.<br /> <br /> No matter the reason, and again with the idea of no exhausting listings, I see no need for any particular NPC or even a big number of them to have this specific Gift, even if in practice most PCs should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Septs have a store of Talens and Fetishes that are given on a temporary basis is in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't mean every sept has access to every given Fetishe. I think level 1-2 Fetishes may even be regarded that way (most septs, or at least most septs in relevant contexts, would have access to some or procure it and get a couple if they don't), but above that things get ever more obscure in regards to specific fetishes. Sure, the sept has high level Fetishes, just not necessarily that particular one.<br /> <br /> And sept-kept Fetishes are even more relevant when discussing character sheets because, precisely given their access to sept troves, a character not having a given Fetishe in their sheet doesn't mean they don't have access to that Fetishe if they want or need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T13:29:59-07:00","id":1477473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477460#post1477460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In absolutely any RPG there's a huge difference between what a player can do and what the NPCs should look like, specially what should be the default among them. PCs are special by definition and have access to things based on game balance and game needs for special characters. NPCs are story elements, and standard NPCs are setting elements.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> So, while you can build such characters and they're perfectly valid, as a setting premise they're probably exceedingly rare, unique or currently non-existent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is completely true. PCs are special because they are specifically designed to fulfill whatever need of the player (to roleplay an intriguing concept, to explore a metaplot element, to be a unique snowflake to make them feel special, to live out a power fantasy, etc.) and not something organic that develops like in real life. Ideally, a setting should be a living world that the ST tries to roleplay realistically based on the setting and genre conventions. PCs often aren't representative of the setting when taken as a large group.<br /> <br /> This is more easily seen in LARP than tabletop, because in tabletop games, STs run most of the game world and she can make sure the NPCs portray the setting as a whole. Even if there is something strange and unusual about a sept of local Garou (or vampires, or whatever), she can establish a rationale why this local group is different and have the NPCs farther away react appropriately. In LARP (and online games with many players), most of the characters are the PCs themselves with only a few actual NPCs. And while LARPs are fun, the end result is that most LARP groups of PCs often do not meet expectations of the setting as portrayed by the books.<br /> <br /> So in LARP/online games, what we usually see is every member of the Silver Fangs be decent, capable leaders who display modern or post-modern sensibilities. We'd have no idea that the tribe, collectively, is supposed to be a bunch of inbred derelicts leading the Garou Nation to disaster because of class prejudices and hidebound devotion to tradition. Shadow Lords might have a dangerous edge to them, but we don't see a bunch of underhanded conspirators willing to use lies, murder, and working with Wyrm minions to accomplish their goals. All the Bone Gnawers are competent, loyal Garou who truly honor the Litany (even if rough and dirty looking), not mostly a bunch of demoralized, resentful, screw ups or Rabble that just don't care. Or PCs that actually treat Metis as bad as they're supposed to be treated. That's because those tribal descriptions best fit for antagonists (NPCs). Players usually want to portray more heroic protagonists. (And STs often don't allow certain concepts if they feel it'd be disruptive to the game. They don't want to deal with some jackass ruining things simply because &quot;it's my character concept!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Or why a quarter of the game is comprised of Ahrouns with the Huge Size merit. Or why most Kinfolk PCs are special in the sense of having Gnosis, Sorcerer Paths, or some other power. Or how almost everyone has high amounts of Pure Breed despite the setting saying that is dying out. Because individual players want the benefits of that. In a tabletop game, having one PC like that is OK. The character is unusual, but every NPC is usually normal so the setting overall meets expectations established by the corebook. But in LARP/online, many players have the same idea, and it strains credibility that there'd be eight Ahrouns who are all 7' tall and weigh 400 lbs of lean muscle in homid just hanging out at this specific sept. (And they're always Ahrouns. I have yet to see a Ragabash or Theurge who has the Huge Size Merit, because the power fantasy here is to play a huge, bad ass warrior. Not a Glasswalker Ragabash who plays basketball on the weekends and has to go to to the Tall &amp; Fat store to buy his clothes so he can show up to work Monday as a forensics accountant.) So in these games, it just sticks out like a sore thumb. It's just not believable as a setting element. But hey, it's a game, so you roll your eyes and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T13:35:31-07:00","id":1477474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Fostern Ragabash would seriously give up on what's probably the best tracking power for the cost in the entire cWoD (It's just 6XP)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody. I call it the &quot;one of the worst defined powers around&quot;-Gift.<br /> Player: &quot;Wait, I can find anyone of whom I know at least a tiny bit of information about?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Well, yeah.&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;So, I track the person who murdered the guy at whose corpse I'm looking.&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Well, that kind of breaks the whole murder-mystery genre. Luckily W20 added 'even a nickname, initials, or crude description' to the description of the needed information, so just knowing that the person is a murderer as a self referring information is not enough....&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;But crude description is enough, right? So, I shift lupus and catch the persons scent. That should be easy enough. Trained dogs can do all kinds of amazing stuff with scent, right?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Sure, roll Perception + Enigmas against 8.&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;So, the perp is actively hiding, heh? Well, no success. Let's try again in a few hours. The perp will need to sleep at some point and I bet he's not splitting dice pools to actively hiding while taking a nap, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> If there was no Ragabash, Black Fury or Red Talon in my pack, I'd pay the 10XP for that Gift at any moment...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, IME, WtA is the opposite when it comes to what played PCs look like to what experienced stated NPCs look like. There's a number of reasons for this, but especially since gaining Backgrounds, Renown, Rank, and Rites are all things that take in-play actions without having dedicated XP costs, and don't have the &quot;size of town and what's available in them&quot; issue thanks to Septs and Moonbridges, playing from start generally gets you way more than coming in with mid-game with some extra dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you came up with the idea to make getting Backgrounds part of the &quot;Family Tragedy&quot; roll. Besides that, we know Moots take place monthly and therefore renown conversion from temp to permanent is at that rate. Rite teaching/learning has no time periods given, but fluff indicates that students have to prove their worth before being taught.<br /> Still, the availability and rate of accumulation of non-XP related character abilities varies heavily from ST/troupe to ST/troupe. It is hard to give any guidelines there, for any NPC of higher rank has to match what is appropriate for the chronicle in question.<br /> <br /> In our LARP game, everything has to be bought with XP at character creation, even backgrounds (they are handled like abilities XP-cost-wise). That is also true for the Rituals Background, determining the Rites a character knows. So, when creating higher level characters, they buy this background higher, to get more rites. Renown isn't tracked numerically, but left to the players. Starting Rank (as well as starting XP) is dependent on negotiations with the ST team, anyway.<br /> Talen &quot;recepies&quot; known to a character who has &quot;Rite of Binding&quot; is also completely dependent on negotiations with the ST team.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sense Wyrm is in-splat for one Breed, one Auspice, and <b>five</b> living Tribes. It's the most commonly accessible Gift in the game (131/190 possible combinations of Breed/Auspice/Tribe get you Sense Wyrm as in-splat at least once). If you have it despite that, why shouldn't you use it? Perception and Occult are not exclusively useful to any splat. Like a lot of sensory powers, the more people that have it and roll it the better, because it increases the odds of a good roll by one of them; even if not the statistically best suited.<br /> [...]<br /> Sense Wyrm isn't perfect, but still incredibly useful. Obviously like any rolled Gift having dice is good (but as noted it's not a hard pool for Garou to justify), and &quot;understanding&quot; is imparted as part of the learning process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the way the ST/troupe handles the Gift and what extra-sensory input it delivers. The statement I answered to was referencing was about detecting the maine enemies and that is not what the gift does. It provides clues for further examination and investigation. And sure, if you have it, use it. But if you aren't the Perception+Occult specialist and waste the packs time or trigger events that bring harm to person simply because you can't interpret what you perceive then it is your Wisdom-loss.<br /> But, clearly, being wrong also contributes to learning and surely usage of the Gift by more then one person can lead to better results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477466#post1477466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Septs have a store of Talens and Fetishes that are given on a temporary basis is in the books. Lots of Fetishes are situational in their applications, and are best kept communally and attuned for an in-depth mission before being returned, rather than held by one Garou that might not need it lots of the time they have it. Monkey Puzzles are a perfect example of the kind of Fetish that makes sense to share. As a rank 4 Fetish it's not common, and most Garou don't need it's effects frequently, so the Sept is better having one or two they can assign to a pack when needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference?<br /> I mean, Talens, sure. That's what they are made for. Fetishes, I can recall only fetishes for offices or semi-permanent once, for like a mission lasting several months, not on a day-to-day basis, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T03:26:26-07:00","id":1477523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477469#post1477469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even level 1 Gifts must be taught by specific spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They have to be taught be various classes of spirits. :Outside of specifically rare and hard to get Gifts, you only need a spirit that qualifies. Keeping in mind that &quot;ancestor spirits&quot; is the most common (over 60 Gifts, almost twenty more then next closest), and every Sept has those. Sense Wyrm can be taught by <b>any Gaian spirit</b>. So that's not exactly a tough restriction.<br /> <br /> A Gaian aligned wolf ancestor spirit... which lots of Septs are going to have at least one of around, can teach almost 125 Gifts. And, generally, you don't have to find Incarnae or their direct high level avatars. Any spirit of the right associations will do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or even that the sheets for experienced characters should be read as exhausting for lists of powers/fetishes instead of examples. </div> </div> </div>While it is fine, in play, to house rule the official sheets of NPCs to suit the needs of your games, it's not viable in a forum discussion about official Garou characters vs. vampire elders.<br /> <br /> If the sheet doesn't say that the powers listed aren't exhaustive, then those are the powers the character officially has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes a lot of difference, but doesn't eliminates the core argument that reaching a given point in the game with whatever the game threw at you is far different from being able to pick and choose what you'll have from the lists in the books, freely. </div> </div> </div>The point you're making is irrelevant. &quot;Starting level&quot; characters are not, for example, able to take anything they want freely. Also, to be frank, the whole, &quot;Well I can show that it's no 100% the case that what you said is always true all the time, therefore whatever I say is right,&quot; thing isn't actually a point to make. It's just bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even for in-game searches the PC's have the advantage of the players knowing such lists, so they have far more intimacy with the idea and the process than the characters, specially the NPCs, necessarily would. </div> </div> </div>There's a whole Auspice and at least three Sept offices where knowing the right spirits to teach things should be part of their skill sets. The games never describe this as highly difficult or secretive knowledge in general within Garou society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it being in-splat doesn't mean it being what you got to pick. </div> </div> </div>It might not be what you start with, but at 3 XP, and any Gaian spirit can teach it to you in an hour, not picking it up eventually is silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I see no need for any particular NPC or even a big number of them to have this specific Gift, even if in practice most PCs should. </div> </div> </div>Because the separation between PC and NPC in WtA isn't vast enough to justify them having radically different approaches to what Gifts/etc. to learn. The Garou are a military society engaged in active warfare for generations. There are certain skills that most soldiers pick up, and leadership is promoted from within, so the leadership NPCs were once Cliaths in the PCs shoes themselves (and generally not that long ago, because Garou don't live that long).<br /> <br /> In Garou society, there is no skipping boot camp and jumping straight into a commissioned officer program. Everyone starts as a grunt, and gets promoted based on the same general criteria for their Auspice. Making it to Adren or higher makes those NPCs exceptional, just like the PCs, because surviving to that point is exceptional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't mean every sept has access to every given Fetishe. </div> </div> </div>Did I say it did?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sept-kept Fetishes are even more relevant when discussing character sheets because, precisely given their access to sept troves, a character not having a given Fetishe in their sheet doesn't mean they don't have access to that Fetishe if they want or need to. </div> </div> </div>So... yeah?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477474#post1477474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was no Ragabash, Black Fury or Red Talon in my pack, I'd pay the 10XP for that Gift at any moment...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. How many official Garou sheets have it even though it's obviously that good?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, you came up with the idea to make getting Backgrounds part of the &quot;Family Tragedy&quot; roll. </div> </div> </div>What does that have to do with this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides that, we know Moots take place monthly and therefore renown conversion from temp to permanent is at that rate. </div> </div> </div>Sept's have a monthly moot. There's a whole list of other moots where the rite can theoretically be performed throughout the year; Hearings are more frequently held in Septs than full Moots and explicitly are used to reward Renown. And the spirits can just make it happen if they feel like the Garou deserves it (giving the ST permission to allow for Renown and Rank advancement in games that aren't bound tightly to Septs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rite teaching/learning has no time periods given,... </div> </div> </div>One week per level of Rite for each roll to learn it..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, the availability and rate of accumulation of non-XP related character abilities varies heavily from ST/troupe to ST/troupe. It is hard to give any guidelines there, for any NPC of higher rank has to match what is appropriate for the chronicle in question. </div> </div> </div>And? My point was just that you can't actually make the comparison being made of a played D&amp;D character vs. a new one made with at the same level as the PC joining mid-game, due to the very different mechanics at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In our LARP game... </div> </div> </div>How are your house rules relevant to this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends on the way the ST/troupe handles the Gift and what extra-sensory input it delivers. </div> </div> </div>The Gift is not as vague as you make it sound. Detecting a fomor in the next room is a listed example of what the Gift is capable of revealing. So, even if Sense Wyrm isn't &quot;Detect Evil,&quot; it is still, &quot;Gauge the strength of the taint and number of Wyrm manifestations nearby enough successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fomori are definitely a main enemy of the Garou, and Sense Wyrm lets you detect them through walls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It provides clues for further examination and investigation. </div> </div> </div>It does both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Talens, sure. That's what they are made for. Fetishes, I can recall only fetishes for offices or semi-permanent once, for like a mission lasting several months, not on a day-to-day basis, though. </div> </div> </div>I said mission-to-mission, not day-to-day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 03-27-2022, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T02:10:17-07:00","id":1477573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. How many official Garou sheets have it even though it's obviously that good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, or they think of the Gift as to powerful due to unspecific limitations, too...<br /> Or they want to not create a situation, where every Cliath pack will ask the fostern NPC to track someone for them, for the glory of Gaia and so on....<br /> <br /> But mainly, it is due to the fact, that most NPCs have Gifts and other powers from their tribe, auspice and breed, exclusively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does that have to do with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referencing to the fact that the way players or npcs gain background po\u00ednts in play is highly subjective on the STs part. When creating a seasoned NPC you grant backgrounds as you thing suitable, there is no real guideline for that. An Glass Walker information broker will have more contacts and allies as a Red Talon who spend all days in the woods. The Red Talon will not necessarily have Fetishes and Numen to compensate for that. Some NPCs just have less backgrounds.<br /> <br /> High ranking NPCs are also a tool to flesh out a story - they are not necessarily build al templates for STs.<br /> That is where the templates from the TBs differ, for those are meant to show cliath starting characters (although they sometimes don't hold up to the rules).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sept's have a monthly moot. There's a whole list of other moots where the rite can theoretically be performed throughout the year; Hearings are more frequently held in Septs than full Moots and explicitly are used to reward Renown. And the spirits can just make it happen if they feel like the Garou deserves it (giving the ST permission to allow for Renown and Rank advancement in games that aren't bound tightly to Septs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Other gatherings might be an option. Not sure if spirits can just award rank, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One week per level of Rite for each roll to learn it..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? My point was just that you can't actually make the comparison being made of a played D&amp;D character vs. a new one made with at the same level as the PC joining mid-game, due to the very different mechanics at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are your house rules relevant to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>LARPs often have the need to come up with rules to build more seasoned characters or NPCs. Therefore the mechanic is an example. I'm sure MET has it's own guidelines (it has been a while since I build a character for the game in New Orleans).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gift is not as vague as you make it sound. Detecting a fomor in the next room is a listed example of what the Gift is capable of revealing. So, even if Sense Wyrm isn't &quot;Detect Evil,&quot; it is still, &quot;Gauge the strength of the taint and number of Wyrm manifestations nearby enough successes.&quot;<br /> [..]<br /> Fomori are definitely a main enemy of the Garou, and Sense Wyrm lets you detect them through walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, well... maybe.<br /> I mean, the gift states it requires concentration. It doesn't state that it requires targeting... Unless you read on page 278 of W20 where the sentence<br /> &quot;<i>Attempts to use Sense Wyrm <b>on</b> the fomor suffer increased difficulty (10).</i>&quot;<br /> Could indicate that you have to specify the target. If that was the case, is places, as well as people and objects can be targeted, but one would argue the reach is limited to the current scene, right?<br /> <br /> So, while there is the sentence that a fomori in the next room's wyrm taint is sensed at difficulty 6, it doesn't say that the gift works though walls, or even all types of walls.<br /> Will it work from the living room to the kitchen in the next room? Probably.<br /> Will it work from the street through the store window into the bakery? Possibly<br /> Will it work from the garou standing right next to the window-less thick brick outer wall of the house to the interior? Maybe not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, page 275 states:<br /> &quot;<i>Sense Wyrm works best as a way to generate story hooks, not as a faultless \u201cWyrm Detector\u201d that enables the Garou to spot the evil-doer and rip him limb from limb before the story has even begun.</i>&quot;<br /> So, given sufficient successes it sure provides clues that overwhelmingly determine the wyrm creature as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477523#post1477523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said mission-to-mission, not day-to-day.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, limited to missions that with due diligence appear to reasonably last longer than a few hours....?<br /> I mean certain missions can be as short as doing some sept chores, while others are endeavours lasting months or years....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T03:00:35-07:00","id":1477574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477573#post1477573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, or they think of the Gift as to powerful due to unspecific limitations, too...<br /> Or they want to not create a situation, where every Cliath pack will ask the fostern NPC to track someone for them, for the glory of Gaia and so on....<br /> <br /> But mainly, it is due to the fact, that most NPCs have Gifts and other powers from their tribe, auspice and breed, exclusively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you name a single Fostern or higher ranked character with Sense/Pulse of the Prey as in-splat for them, that actually has it? And it's a core book power, not some some obscure one off like Cleaving Hoof for assassin Children of Gaia Rabash to abuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was referencing to the fact that the way players or npcs gain background po\u00ednts in play is highly subjective on the STs part. </div> </div> </div>Which:<br /> <br /> 1) Doesn't really add anything to the tangent being argued and,<br /> 2) Adds even less to the general topic of official Garou fights with other supernaturals seeming to end with the Garou getting Worfed all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> High ranking NPCs are also a tool to flesh out a story - they are not necessarily build al templates for STs. </div> </div> </div>Nobody claimed otherwise. The claims are:<br /> <br /> 1) The officially stated high Rank NPCs have really bad stats for what they're supposed to be capable of doing.<br /> 2) The approach to stating WtA NPCs needs to more closely resemble ow PCs are built because of the differences in setting and culture. An Adren Glass Walker information broker should look different from an Adren Red Talon, sure, but they should look a lot more like what a Cliath PC Glass Walker information broker wants to look like once they get that kind of Rank and XP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other gatherings might be an option. Not sure if spirits can just award rank, though. </div> </div> </div>I said Renown. And yes, you can have 10 Renown converted to 1 Permanent Renown because the ST decides it to be so without the Rite. This is supposed to be rare of course, but it is something the books say is possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LARPs often have the need to come up with rules to build more seasoned characters or NPCs. </div> </div> </div>Again, the thread is about official Garou NPC fights. It doesn't matter how LARPs address making high Ranking NPCs for their own games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, well... maybe. </div> </div> </div>The Gift might be awkwardly worded, but you can't deny that it can be used to detect enemies that are strongly of the Wyrm that you might not be able to sense with your normal senses, and thus is incredibly useful for any Garou to pick up as warriors in the fight against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you read on page 278 of W20<br /> ...<br /> Yet, page 275 states: </div> </div> </div>I think you gave your page citations off.<br /> <br /> These are both in the Dramatic Systems section and don't reference the Gift. I can't find either of the passages you're talking about in W20 core by searching for &quot;Sense Wyrm.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, limited to missions that with due diligence appear to reasonably last longer than a few hours....?<br /> I mean certain missions can be as short as doing some sept chores, while others are endeavours lasting months or years.... </div> </div> </div>Missions as dictated by the Sept officer of jurisdiction (usually the Warder). <br /> <br /> What point are you even trying to make here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T04:12:11-07:00","id":1477576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477574#post1477574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you name a single Fostern or higher ranked character with Sense/Pulse of the Prey as in-splat for them, that actually has it? And it's a core book power, not some some obscure one off like Cleaving Hoof for assassin Children of Gaia Rabash to abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from the top of my head, no.<br /> But isn't that kind of the point. While rules allow to take such powers, within the game universe it is rarely done?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477574#post1477574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody claimed otherwise. The claims are:<br /> <br /> 1) The officially stated high Rank NPCs have really bad stats for what they're supposed to be capable of doing.<br /> 2) The approach to stating WtA NPCs needs to more closely resemble ow PCs are built because of the differences in setting and culture. An Adren Glass Walker information broker should look different from an Adren Red Talon, sure, but they should look a lot more like what a Cliath PC Glass Walker information broker wants to look like once they get that kind of Rank and XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. But could it be, that the authors have a very different idea bout the power level of garou of a given rank in relation to their experience-bought attributes/abilities/gifts than players do?<br /> Could it be the case that these are also different in regards to what a werewolf author thinks of a garou NPC in ralations to a vampire NPC and what a vampire author thinks about these.<br /> <br /> A werewolf author might have and Adren or such NPC be a bit more grounded and not have maxed out stats to demonstrate that there is still something to aim for and that the NPC is capable of failure and leave the PCs space to shine in comparison. Also the werewolf author might think of a vampire NPC and the combat prowess thereof in terms of the core books antagonist section, with werewolf stats, rather than the fully fleshed out VtM character it could be...<br /> <br /> Same might be true for a VtM author. Using Celerity and stuff like that to interpolate a seasoned garous capabilities might of set what we as WtA players think of a seasoned garou character.<br /> <br /> I get the 2nd claim, but the problem is, that it is kind of subjective what a player wants his, for example, Glass Walker to look like once the Rank and XP are there, because the time it takes to reach a certain rank and the number of XP available by then aren't quantified - and possibly most PCs earn ranks and exp faster than what authors might think the Setting would allow....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477574#post1477574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gift might be awkwardly worded, but you can't deny that it can be used to detect enemies that are strongly of the Wyrm that you might not be able to sense with your normal senses, and thus is incredibly useful for any Garou to pick up as warriors in the fight against the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't deny that - depending on how the usage works with a given ST.<br /> I, personally, as ST, would think the Gift is useful but if you have not the dice pool to score sufficient successes it most often will tell you &quot;There is taint&quot; and that won't bring you that far. I mean sure, a player can think &quot;This is most likely a fomori in the next room, for if it was something different, like lingering taint of tainted fast food, the difficulty might be higher and I would not have detected it.&quot; but that is kind of meta gaming, if the ST doesn't roll covertly and the difficulty is known to the player and so on....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477574#post1477574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you gave your page citations off.<br /> <br /> These are both in the Dramatic Systems section and don't reference the Gift. I can't find either of the passages you're talking about in W20 core by searching for &quot;Sense Wyrm.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. Sorry. My Acrobat Reader jumped into the revised Corebook tab and I searched there instead of W20....<br /> In W20 the noted &quot;use Sense Wyrm on someone&quot; choice of words is found with the Smell Fear BSD gift...still.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477574#post1477574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Missions as dictated by the Sept officer of jurisdiction (usually the Warder).<br /> What point are you even trying to make here?</div> </div> </div> </div>That fetishes are given to garou, who attune themselves to it, for extended periods of times. Something that is assumed to be not taking as long as is felt suitable, will not be a mission for which a fetish will be provided...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T12:40:15-07:00","id":1477594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477576#post1477576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not from the top of my head, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But isn't that kind of the point. While rules allow to take such powers, within the game universe it is rarely done? </div> </div> </div>The problem is the game does not posit this as the state of the game universe. The core book Gifts (outside of W20's inclusion of Camp Gifts) are supposed to be the most common Gifts known. A core book Fostern Ragabash Gift is supposed to be something a large number of Fostern and higher Ranked Ragabash have learned. The stated NPCs are not built to this assumption, despite books saying this is the case.<br /> <br /> If the books said learning Gifts in general was rare, you might have a case here. But they don't. W20 says that Gifts are literally the difference between the Garou losing the war against the Wyrm ages ago, and them ever standing a chance. Having Gifts is that important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But could it be, that the authors have a very different idea bout the power level of garou of a given rank in relation to their experience-bought attributes/abilities/gifts than players do? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter why. It matters what the end result is, and that's official NPCs that are woefully under powered for their narrative functions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...not have maxed out stats... </div> </div> </div>Please stop with the strawmen already. How many times am I going to have to call you out on saying things I didn't say?<br /> <br /> My statement was that an NPC Glasswalker Adren information broker should have a sheet that actually looks like what a PC of the same concept would want to have in the future. I didn't say anything about maxing out stats. Players shouldn't feel like NPCs are jokes because they skipped level 1 in-splat Gifts that are directly in-concept for them to have, or have shit dice-pools for what they're supposed to be good at, or have glaring issues that denote a lack of understanding of the rules (ex: do not use the official stats for Jonas in a stare down challenge, he'll probably lose from having to roll Rage and end up having to break the contest to contain a Frenzy, up his stats slightly so this doesn't happen).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the werewolf author might think of a vampire NPC and the combat prowess thereof in terms of the core books antagonist section, with werewolf stats, rather than the fully fleshed out VtM character it could be. </div> </div> </div>Again, this is irrelevant, and further the point at how easily you can make PCs that are more competent than the official NPCs means the sample VtM-written-with-WtA-rules antagonists are just as flawed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the 2nd claim, but the problem is, that it is kind of subjective... </div> </div> </div>If you get the second claim, than you should understand that subjectivity is acknowledged and even built into its phrasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't deny that - depending on how the usage works with a given ST. </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't deny that, but I'm going to continue to protest it because ST fiat,&quot; is not a good argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...still. </div> </div> </div>Still what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That fetishes are given to garou, who attune themselves to it, for extended periods of times. Something that is assumed to be not taking as long as is felt suitable, will not be a mission for which a fetish will be provided... </div> </div> </div>This doesn't explain anything. Some Fetishes are outright owned by certain Garou (or some similar phrasing like &quot;entrusted by the Tribe,&quot; to be more evocative), others are owned by organizations with the Nation. Those owned communally can be assigned to a Garou based on the needs of the organization.<br /> <br /> What else matters about this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T19:06:03-07:00","id":1477602,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness rules in general don\u2019t do epic combat between powerful creatures very well. It\u2019s because usually offensive scales way faster than defense. In movies or other stories when we think of two supernatural creature of great power fight, they fight for hours, each striking blows and inflicting wounds, but continuing to fight. We see this kind of fight described between Mithras and the werewolf pack or between Ravnos and his various opponents. The rules doesn\u2019t accommodate that. Using WoD rules, one creature goes first and gets 6 attacks each one doing 15 levels of aggravated damage and then the victim only gets 8 dice of soak, so it dies on the first round of combat. The winner is the one who attacks from Obfuscate or drops out of the umbra first. Or to take it to the next level, attack during the daytime with the pack or have your ghouls take a bomb to the Cairn. <br /> <br /> That isn\u2019t as interesting, though, as the epic all night fight. So the fights are described in a way that the rules can\u2019t emulate and almost always this will be in the elder vampire\u2019s favor, since that kind of fight will usually favor the Garou pack over the elder vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T20:39:21-07:00","id":1477612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please stop with the strawmen already. How many times am I going to have to call you out on saying things I didn't say?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a clarification is needed here.<br /> <br /> You made yourself clear enough to me already and I mostly agree. The problem, though, is one of context: the things you said, you said at first in support for lbeaumanior, and <b>they did</b> say the things you're coming off to some as having said. That colored my readings of your posts in this tangent for a time, it may still be coloring <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>'s and maybe others, can't say for sure. lbeaumanior, in the way they wrote, came off as defending full on optimization for NPCs, not just making them earn their purported place (that last one, I'm on full support, but official sheets are that messy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T23:07:33-07:00","id":1477617,"title":"","content":"Ibeaumanior doesn't seem to be saying that NPCs should be full optimized, but they should actually be built to reflect the rules of the game better. Optimization came in, in how you can optimized starting level, or near starting level PCs and utterly destroy the canon official stated Rank 6 Legendary Garou. A Legendary Garou should not be ganked by a starting level pack any more than a Methuselah vampire should be by a pack of neonates, no matter how min-maxed or optimized they are.<br /> <br /> The VtM authors seem to recognize this and made sure to liberally assign dots to high level NPCs (which is easier with Disciplines). The WtA authors did not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T01:57:27-07:00","id":1477620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is the game does not posit this as the state of the game universe. The core book Gifts (outside of W20's inclusion of Camp Gifts) are supposed to be the most common Gifts known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? I can't remember reading this. I'd argue the core book is supposed to show a broad range of Gifts that lets players get a feeling of the splat even without the TBs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A core book Fostern Ragabash Gift is supposed to be something a large number of Fostern and higher Ranked Ragabash have learned. The stated NPCs are not built to this assumption, despite books saying this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Red Talon TB has two stats, Hot-Eye has the Gift, the Rank 6 (who has 'Elder' written in brackets after the 6) doesn't have the Gift.<br /> <br /> In Rage Across the Amazon all Furies have the Gift, but both Fostern Ragabash have not. But maybe tracking isn't so much the problem as are machine guns, therefore the choice of Jam Technology for Roshen makes sense....<br /> <br /> In Rite of Passion it is on the list of Gifts the BSD should pick from. From an NPC standpoint one in the pack would be enough to track the PCs so the other BSD could pick other Gifts for variety. But they could all have it, if you prefer...<br /> <br /> Rage across New York finds the Gift for the Lupus Athro, but not the two Ragabash. But Blissful Ignorance and Taken the Forgotten are also solid picks, depending on what the Ragabash primarily does.<br /> <br /> Past Live doesn't have Ragabash stats, but the Lupus has the Gift.<br /> <br /> Rage across Egypt has the Gift for the Ragabash Elder Metis, but not for the Cliath, obviously.<br /> <br /> The Gift is also prominent among Balam and Khan, but I think it is lower Rank. Still, Drivethru Text search found it, so I mention it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, the Gift does appear, but some Adren have one or two Auspice Fostern Gifts at the most, and there are other solid picks, so your expectation to see the Gift more often is possibly based on a game world that is not similar to what the (especially early edition) authors thought the world was.<br /> <br /> I mean, the sheer number of Gifts per character is significantly lower that what I would expect from any PC at that rank. Most Adren, in my game experience, have plenty of XP to buy Fostern Gifts before even making it to Adren, but official NPCs rarely have more than four.... and they often take from Breed/Auspice/Tribe, so there is only one or two auspice fostern gifts in their stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the books said learning Gifts in general was rare, you might have a case here. But they don't. W20 says that Gifts are literally the difference between the Garou losing the war against the Wyrm ages ago, and them ever standing a chance. Having Gifts is that important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there too, might have been a paradigm shift. Back in 2nd Edition there was:<br /> &quot;<i>If a high ranking Theurge, such as Glass Walker Roger Daly, has 10 Gifts, while the Cliath Stargazer Galliard Howard Koar has three, how many might a mere Kinfolk possess?</i>&quot;<br /> Roger Daly being a fricking Elder with 10 Gifts.... Appearing to be in his late 50s early 60s - this means he learned a Gift about every four years or so....<br /> <br /> Other NPCs share the relatively low number of Gifts.<br /> <br /> I think we could make an argument that early WW authors did see their WtA-world significantly less magical....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter why. It matters what the end result is, and that's official NPCs that are woefully under powered for their narrative functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What narrative functions?<br /> Being quest-giver?<br /> Being mentors?<br /> Being teachers?<br /> Being authority figures?<br /> <br /> I mean, they are sept office holders and such. Should they be able to hold that positions with they low stats? Well, if the enemies have stats on the same level, then true, they should, could and apparently are...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please stop with the strawmen already. How many times am I going to have to call you out on saying things I didn't say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, aside from Gifts, Rites and Backgrounds you can have multiple times like Fetish, what else is there...<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 4 (6/8/7/5), Dexterity 4 (4/5/6/6),<br /> Stamina 5 (7/8/8/8), Charisma 4, Manipulation 3 (2/0/0/0),<br /> Appearance 4 (3/0/4/4), Perception 4, Intelligence 4, Wits 5<br /> <br /> Literally each attribute increase that Roger Daly has to make him more capable is maxing it out. Abilities have a bit more potential and Rage, Willpower and Gnosis are abyssal for an Elder (or the author thought they were also 1 to 5), sure...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My statement was that an NPC Glasswalker Adren information broker should have a sheet that actually looks like what a PC of the same concept would want to have in the future. I didn't say anything about maxing out stats. Players shouldn't feel like NPCs are jokes because they skipped level 1 in-splat Gifts that are directly in-concept for them to have, or have shit dice-pools for what they're supposed to be good at, or have glaring issues that denote a lack of understanding of the rules (ex: do not use the official stats for Jonas in a stare down challenge, he'll probably lose from having to roll Rage and end up having to break the contest to contain a Frenzy, up his stats slightly so this doesn't happen).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that certain stats are not necessarily well thought through.<br /> <br /> And, I imagine, some authors want a given stat to represent some thing, like Rage for combat prowess (a must pick because of multiple action rules), but didn't realise the other implications this stat would have, or did judge them differently...<br /> <br /> On the other hand there might be a gap between what you, me or players in general think of a dice pool that is adequate and what the authors think, or thought back in the day....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't deny that, but I'm going to continue to protest it because ST fiat,&quot; is not a good argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often have you rolled Sense Wyrm with one success and then had your character kill a person who had taint on him but was innocent or wasted time on following clues to discover the pointlessness?<br /> The usefulness of the Gift, even if used RAW, is totally dependent on what you thing the game world and the rules governing taint look like in practice.<br /> <br /> I mean, there is a mention of fast food bought at Pentex's subsidiary is transferring taint to people. No rules given how long that lasts. So, cities are basically full of false positives whenever there is a fast food store of that branch open. And does that extend to other Pentex subsidiaries as well. If there was taint on every kid playing with Tellus or Black Dog games, a lot of kids are false positives as well...<br /> <br /> Simply by weighting certain sentences in the rules and Setting descriptions differently, the Gift looses party of its usefulness. So, I don't deny that the Gift finds wyrm tainted enemies, enemies other senses might have not caught and that is can be extremely useful. But the last part is depending on how your ST handles the game world more than other aspects of the Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like revised, there is still a mention in W20 depicting Sense Wyrm aimed on a specific target, rather than at a scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477594#post1477594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What else matters about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>That the respect for the fetish stays intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T03:01:24-07:00","id":1477622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477620#post1477620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Maybe spend some more time going back and reading some books like the Players Guides and ST books instead of constantly trying to undermine what I'm saying for reasons I'm can't figure out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue... </div> </div> </div>You'd argue that your opinion is right? Wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, the sheer number of Gifts per character is significantly lower that what I would expect from any PC at that rank. </div> </div> </div>Then what are you even arguing against?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we could make an argument that early WW authors did see their WtA-world significantly less magical.... </div> </div> </div>So what? How many ways do I need to say that I don't care why the WW authors made the decisions they did? I'm not arguing the stats in the books are not what's in the books. I'm saying the stats in the books are badly done for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What narrative functions? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that certain stats are not necessarily well thought through. </div> </div> </div>Again, what are you even arguing against then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How often have you rolled Sense Wyrm with one success and then had your character kill a person who had taint on him but was innocent or wasted time on following clues to discover the pointlessness? </div> </div> </div>None of my characters have ever killed a character solely based on rolling 1 success on Sense Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I cannot count the number of times I've had characters run down leads that were pointless, Sense Wyrm or some other thing (including just really high Investigation stats). But that's generally a ST problem.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why this matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The usefulness of the Gift, even if used RAW, is totally dependent on what you thing the game world and the rules governing taint look like in practice. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in the game that can't be made worthless depending on how the ST runs the game.<br /> <br /> And still, none of this matters to the specific complaint that you apparently agree with that the WtA NPC tend to be stated poorly, or the wider issue of Garou not getting to flex in crossover conflicts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That the respect for the fetish stays intact. </div> </div> </div>Meaningless.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Also, before you do a point by point response to all that?<br /> <br /> What the fuck is you goal here? I'm serious. Are you just playing Devil's Advocate? Are you trying to make some point that's actually relevant to the thread? Are you just getting off on nitpicking and using the ambiguity of bad writing over multiple edition to needle people? Because I can't come up with an actual positive charitable rationale at this point, and it's getting grating.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T07:55:25-07:00","id":1477628,"title":"","content":"I don't think the quality of the NPC character sheets matter that much for the thread's problem because I hardly think any fiction author ever even considered those sheets. Indeed, I'm not sure all of them were even aware that Gifts are a thing to begin with.<br /> <br /> While I'd address both problem to the same source, they're individually irrelevant to one another. And it doesn't even matter in the end, because the actual issue persists of bad writing and cheap storytelling making the Garou get the short stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T13:32:50-07:00","id":1477642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the fuck is you goal here? I'm serious. Are you just playing Devil's Advocate? Are you trying to make some point that's actually relevant to the thread? Are you just getting off on nitpicking and using the ambiguity of bad writing over multiple edition to needle people? Because I can't come up with an actual positive charitable rationale at this point, and it's getting grating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know yet.<br /> I'm entertaining the idea that very different troupes I played the tabletop version of the game with and the different LARP games I played with all had certain pre-conceptions about the game, as well as you and I, and that these aren't necessarily how the authors or developer guidelines (which I assume the authors were given) think the game or the setting are.<br /> <br /> Circling back to the Original Question, there doesn't seem to be a lot of canonical material around.<br /> <br /> It might be simply the case because Garou in VtM narratives serve a different purpose than vampires in a WtA narrative.<br /> In VtM garou are the big bad, and if they are defeated it is to showcase the badass-ness of some vampire character. Having garou caged in the Succubus Club, for example. In a WtA narrative vampires don't have a vice versa place. They are annoying to the garou for they tend to hide and run and for anyone who wants to tell a WtA story, or set up a scenario outside such 1st Edition experiments like the Vancouver sourcebook, doesn't make it very interesting with vampires. They use fomori or banes or BSD.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> As for the point by point part of the answer...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Maybe spend some more time going back and reading some books like the Players Guides and ST books instead of constantly trying to undermine what I'm saying for reasons I'm can't figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you provide a reference for the statement that pre-W20 core book Gifts are supposed to be the most commonly known Gifts in the game?<br /> <br /> And do you mean that these are the Gifts most members of the respective Breed/Auspice/Tribe have learned or known to the general public?<br /> Because I would think that &quot;Aura of Confidence&quot;, &quot;Fatale Flaw&quot; and &quot;Seizing the Edge&quot; are Gifts the Shadowlords don't want anyone to know about, while the Get of Fenris don't care if tales of their heroics mention that they can call upon the Might of Thor.<br /> <br /> I can see, that they are the Gifts most members of these splats learn, sure. But since a character belongs to three splats and authors seem to evenly distribute Gifts and not to many of those, a lot of characters don't know all the Core book Gifts of their splats even at Cliath level, and not even those that are potentially 'must haves'.<br /> Sure, they cost only 3XP, but the in-character hustle to get them might be another thing. I mean, if one uses one of Axis Mundis several options on how to handle Gift learning...<br /> <br /> Post W20 Sourcebooks seem to have more Gifts for NPCs, though.<br /> Adren are found with 9 to 16 Gifts, average 12,6 (not including Skinner) and averaging 10,4 Gifts with the Skindancers.<br /> Athro I found have 8 to 11 Gifts (yes, the examples I found have less then the Adren NPCs).<br /> The Skinner Reborn scores 21 Gifts, far exceeding the Nightmaster...<br /> <br /> How many Gifts do played characters at a certain rank have would be a funny new topic, possibly showing some correlation to the play style...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what? How many ways do I need to say that I don't care why the WW authors made the decisions they did? I'm not arguing the stats in the books are not what's in the books. I'm saying the stats in the books are badly done for the game.<br /> [....]<br /> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I fail to see how.<br /> You state that they don't fulfil their narrative function, because of their stats.<br /> Do you roll the stats of NPCs to check if they have an answer to a question a player character asks them?<br /> Do you roll their stats when they order the player characters pack on a mission?<br /> Do you roll their instruction skill after a month of teaching the player characters some stuff?<br /> <br /> For I do, occasionally, but never had the feeling that the NPCs failed in their narrative functions, even if I rolled badly for them.<br /> So, I wonder, if there were actual events you experience or is it a general estimate that their stats should not be sufficient for what they do....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what are you even arguing against then?</div> </div> </div> </div>That certain stats have different usages and even if authors are aware of all of the rules of each Gift and Social interaction and combat application and so on, they still would have a problem to formulate the best stats for the way they want the character to be...<br /> Basically, cut the author of character stats some slack.... they might not have been the ones who made the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot count the number of times I've had characters run down leads that were pointless, Sense Wyrm or some other thing (including just really high Investigation stats). But that's generally a ST problem.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why this matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I wanted to illustrate is, that little success on Sense Wyrm can lead to such pointless undertakings which would not happen, if more successes were scored to begin with. Therefore, my conclusion would be, that only those who aim at a decent Sense Wyrm dice pool would bring a benefit to the pack by learning this gift. For others the usefulness is less a given as I felt your argument conveyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477622#post1477622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Werewolves hold great reverence toward fetishes, treating them as honored allies rather than mere tools.<br /> Such is the nature of the pact that binds spirits into fetishes; they are obligated to serve the Garou only as long as they are respected in return.</i><br /> - W20 page 221 (this time I checked, that it is the right PDF)<br /> <br /> For me the mission-per-mission basis, by which a fetish is pulled from the armory and given to a garou who then attunes and forms a spiritual bond between himself and the fetish, feels like not respecting the fetish and indeed degrade it to a mere tool a garou needs for the mission and then hands back. Sure, some pompous ceremony when giving the fetish or returning it can mitigate this, but it simply feels off to me.<br /> If there is a certain type of mission, that requires a certain skill, then their should be a certain garou ready to do the job and that garou should have the fetish that helps with that with him, until he doesn't hold that post any more. That's how I feel about it. Doesn't mean that there aren't fetishes that are exceptions or that some fetishes do not follow this general statement - wouldn't be the first inconsistency in WtA....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T16:15:37-07:00","id":1477650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477628#post1477628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the quality of the NPC character sheets matter that much for the thread's problem because I hardly think any fiction author ever even considered those sheets. Indeed, I'm not sure all of them were even aware that Gifts are a thing to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It matters to the extent that the Worfing of WtA in crossover is only reinforced in the general view of things by making the official canon NPC's stats such that the Garou &quot;shouldn't&quot; be beating other characters because they don't have the ability to do so (not that they can't, but they don't get given the tools WtA has for it).<br /> <br /> Of course, I didn't think my little gripe going to turn into pages of debating on... honestly I'm not even sure what's being debated...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1475101-canonical-garou-vs-vampire-elder-duel?p=1477642#post1477642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, get back to me when you do. I'm not going to keep up a discussion about how I'm wrong but you don't even know why you think I'm wrong for the sake of you figuring it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/